(253, 'SYEDA NARJIS BATOOL KAZMI', 'narjisbatool.batoolk@gmail.com', NULL, 'Urgent Request for Assistance in Filing a Self-Petition for the well-being of My Son, Ali Abbas Khan', 'usa', 'Dear Concern.\r\n\r\nI hope this email finds you well. I am reaching out to you with an urgent request for assistance and guidance regarding filing a self-petition for the well-being of my son, Ali Abbas Khan, a US citizen with Down syndrome. Given the significant challenges we face, I believe this step is crucial for ensuring his further growth and access to essential care.\r\n\r\nAli Abbas was born on April 26, 2010, in Pakistan and has lived with Down syndrome since birth. As a single mother, I have been solely responsible for his care, medical expenses, and education. Unfortunately, his father abandoned us due to his diagnosis and has not fulfilled his responsibilities, leaving me to navigate this journey alone.\r\n\r\nDespite the challenges, I have provided Ali Abbas with extensive therapy, quality education, and opportunities for growth. He is now 14 years old and thriving, yet facing new challenges associated with puberty. The medical and support infrastructure in Pakistan is inadequate to meet his evolving needs, and local doctors cannot provide the specialized guidance required.\r\n\r\nIn 2024, US specialists advised us to attend the National Down Syndrome Convention in Arizona for essential guidance, but my visa applications have been repeatedly denied. This has severely limited our access to the care Ali Abbas needs as a US citizen, which I believe is a grave injustice.\r\n\r\nI am seeking your expertise to file a self-petition that will allow Ali Abbas to access the care and opportunities he is entitled to in the United States. I have previously attempted to consult with attorneys, but their responses were unsatisfactory. I urgently need clarity and a permanent resolution to ensure that my son\'s rights and well-being are protected.\r\n\r\nI am ready to provide any necessary information or documentation to strengthen our case. Your guidance and support would not only help alleviate our current challenges but also secure a brighter future for Ali Abbas.\r\n\r\nThank you for your attention to this matter. I look forward to your response and am hopeful for a positive outcome.\r\n\r\nBest Regards,\r\n\r\nSyeda Narjis Batool Kazmi\r\nCell#; +923009253429', '2024-08-15 08:14:52', '2024-08-15 08:14:52'),
