v id=\"table_id_3\" class=\"table-responsive\"></div>\r\n</figure>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', 'uploads/1725959985_Canada Express Entry Draw Latest News.webp', 'Canadian Express Entry Draw', '2024-09-11', '2024-09-10 09:19:45', '2024-09-10 09:31:17'),
(59, 'Common Mistakes to Avoid When Hiring an Immigration Consultant', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Hiring an immigration consultant can be a valuable asset, but only if you choose the right one. By avoiding common mistakes like falling for unrealistic promises or failing to verify credentials, you can ensure a smooth and successful immigration journey.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Common Mistakes to Avoid When Hiring an Immigration Consultant\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Hiring an immigration consultant can be a valuable asset, but only if you choose the right one. By avoiding common mistakes like falling for unrealistic promises or failing to verify credentials, you can ensure a smooth and successful immigration journey.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1726045258_Common%20Mistakes%20to%20Avoid%20When%20Hiring%20an%20Immigration%20Consultant%20(1).webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<p>Immigrating to a new country is an exciting yet complicated process. Hiring an immigration consultant can make things easier, but it\'s crucial to choose the right one. Unfortunately, many people make mistakes in the hiring process that can lead to delays, financial loss, or even visa denials. This article will help you understand the common mistakes to avoid when hiring an immigration consultant, ensuring your experience is smooth and stress-free.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Lack of Proper Research</strong></h2>\r\n<p>One of the biggest mistakes people make is failing to do their homework. Choosing an immigration consultant without proper research can lead to serious consequences, such as dealing with unqualified or dishonest consultants.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Not Verifying Credentials</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Many clients overlook the importance of verifying their consultant\'s credentials. Just because someone claims to be an immigration expert doesn&rsquo;t mean they are legally allowed to provide immigration services.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Importance of Certification</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>In most countries, immigration consultants must be certified or accredited by a recognized body. For instance, in Canada, they need to be a member of the College of Immigration and Citizenship Consultants (CICC). In other countries, similar licensing organizations exist. It&rsquo;s critical to confirm that the consultant is recognized by such authorities.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>How to Verify Consultant License</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Always check with the relevant authority to ensure your consultant\'s license is legitimate and up-to-date. Most regulatory bodies have an online database where you can quickly look up a consultant&rsquo;s credentials.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Ignoring Client Reviews and Testimonials</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Word of mouth is powerful, but not all testimonials are reliable. It&rsquo;s important to know how to differentiate between genuine reviews and fabricated ones.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>How to Find Reliable Reviews</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Look for reviews on trusted platforms, such as Google, Trustpilot, or LinkedIn, where fake reviews are less likely to appear. Ensure the reviews are detailed and consistent.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Spotting Fake Testimonials</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Beware of overly generic or exaggerated testimonials. If every review sounds too good to be true, it might be.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Falling for Unrealistic Promises</strong></h2>\r\n<p>If a consultant promises you guaranteed success or an abnormally fast process, that\'s a red flag. Immigration is a complex process, and no consultant can guarantee results.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Promises of Guaranteed Success</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Be wary of consultants who claim they can \"guarantee\" a visa approval. While a good consultant can increase your chances, no one can promise success.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>False Claims About Fast-Tracking</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Some consultants may tell you they can expedite your application. However, there is no such thing as fast-tracking beyond the official process.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>How Immigration Timelines Work</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Immigration timelines depend on the country and type of visa, and they vary greatly. A credible consultant will give you a realistic timeframe based on official information.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Red Flags in Promotional Material</strong></h2>\r\n<p>If a consultant&rsquo;s website or advertisements sound too good to be true, they probably are. Stay away from consultants using gimmicky marketing tactics to lure clients.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Paying Large Upfront Fees</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Another common mistake is paying exorbitant fees upfront without understanding the services you\'re receiving.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Why Consultants Charge Fees</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Consultants charge fees for their expertise, but it should be transparent. Avoid those who pressure you into paying large sums right away.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>What to Expect in Terms of Payment Plans</strong></h2>\r\n<p>A legitimate consultant will offer clear payment plans, allowing you to pay in stages rather than demanding everything upfront.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Signs of a Potential Scam</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>If a consultant asks for a substantial amount of money with no clear service outline, it&rsquo;s a sign of a scam. Always ask for a breakdown of fees.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Importance of Written Agreements</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Make sure everything is documented. A written agreement should clearly state the services, fees, and responsibilities of both parties.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Not Understanding the Consultant\'s Role</strong></h2>\r\n<p>A common mistake is misunderstanding what an <a href=\"../\">immigration consultant</a> can and cannot do.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Lack of Communication and Transparency</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Good communication is key to a successful partnership with your consultant. Avoid consultants who are difficult to reach or unclear about the process.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Red Flags of Poor Communication</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>If your consultant takes days to respond to your queries or is vague about the next steps, that&rsquo;s a bad sign.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>The Importance of Regular Updates</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>A reputable consultant will keep you updated on the status of your application and respond promptly to any concerns.</p>\r\n<h2><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>What to Expect in Terms of Professionalism</strong></span></h2>\r\n<p>Look for professionalism in all interactions. This includes clarity in communication, transparency in processes, and respect for deadlines.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Ignoring Red Flags During Initial Consultations</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Your first meeting with an immigration consultant can tell you a lot about their professionalism. Don&rsquo;t ignore red flags.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Pushy Sales Tactics</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Beware of consultants who rush you into signing a contract or paying fees without fully explaining the process. A good consultant will give you time to make an informed decision.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Reluctance to Provide References</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>A trustworthy <a href=\"../news/Canadian-Express-Entry-Draw-911-Candidates-Invited-for-Permanent-Residency-on-September-9-2024\">visa</a> consultant will have no issue providing references or case studies from previous clients.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>How to Conduct Reference Checks</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Reach out to former clients and ask about their experience with the consultant. This will give you a clearer idea of what to expect.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Falling for Phony Immigration Consultants</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Fake or \"ghost\" consultants can cause you immense harm by taking your money without providing legitimate services.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>What Are Ghost Consultants?</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Ghost consultants are unlicensed individuals who pose as immigration experts. They operate without any legal authority and often vanish after collecting fees.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>How to Protect Yourself from Fake Consultants</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Verify your consultant&rsquo;s credentials, ask for a written contract, and avoid dealing with consultants who operate outside official regulatory bodies.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>Conclusion</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Hiring an immigration consultant can be a valuable asset, but only if you choose the right one. By avoiding common mistakes like falling for unrealistic promises or failing to verify credentials, you can ensure a smooth and successful immigration journey.</p>', 'uploads/1726045258_Common Mistakes to Avoid When Hiring an Immigration Consultant (1).webp', 'Common Mistakes to Avoid', '2024-09-11', '2024-09-11 07:43:30', '2024-09-11 09:01:23'),
(60, 'Eligibility Criteria for Canada Business Immigration', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\"The Canada Startup Visa Program is one of the best routes for entrepreneurs looking to settle in Canada while building innovative businesses.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Eligibility Criteria for Canada Business Immigration\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"The Canada Startup Visa Program is one of the best routes for entrepreneurs looking to settle in Canada while building innovative businesses.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1726118889_Eligibility%20Criteria%20for%20Canada%20Business%20Immigration.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<p>Canada has been a beacon for <strong>business-minded individuals</strong> looking to expand their horizons, and the <a href=\"../service/canadian-immigration-services/start-up-visa-program/\">Canada Business Immigration</a> pathway provides numerous opportunities. One such option is the <strong>Start-up Visa Program (SUV)</strong>, which offers a direct route for <strong>innovative entrepreneurs</strong>. Launched in 2013, this program is specifically designed to attract <strong>foreign entrepreneurs</strong> keen to start or grow businesses in Canada.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>General Overview of Canada Business Immigration Program</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>What is the Start-up Visa Program?</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The <strong>Start-up Visa Program</strong> is a Canadian government initiative that aims to bring innovative entrepreneurs to the country. These entrepreneurs are expected to build businesses that:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Are <strong>innovative</strong>,</li>\r\n<li>Can create <strong>jobs</strong> for Canadians,</li>\r\n<li>And have the <strong>potential to compete</strong> on a global scale.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Key Features of the Program</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>This program helps talented entrepreneurs by offering them support and guidance. The ultimate goal is to drive economic growth, encourage job creation, and make Canada a hub for innovative business ideas. The key to success in this program lies in collaboration with designated organizations that help fund and mentor applicants.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Benefits of the Start-up Visa Program</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Why Choose the Start-up Visa Program?</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The <strong>Start-up Visa Program</strong> is not just another immigration pathway; it is a unique opportunity for entrepreneurs to establish themselves in one of the world&rsquo;s most prosperous and stable countries. The benefits include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Fast-track to permanent residency</strong> in Canada.</li>\r\n<li>Access to a <strong>global market</strong> for your business.</li>\r\n<li>Support from <strong>Canada&rsquo;s top investors</strong> and business incubators.</li>\r\n<li>A chance to be a part of Canada&rsquo;s thriving entrepreneurial ecosystem.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>How It Stimulates the Economy</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The program plays a crucial role in the Canadian economy. By bringing in innovative businesses, it:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Creates jobs</strong> for Canadians.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Stimulates innovation</strong> in various industries.</li>\r\n<li>Helps <strong>diversify the economy</strong>, ensuring long-term growth and resilience.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Eligibility Requirements for Applicants</strong></h2>\r\n<p>To qualify for the <strong>Start-up Visa Program</strong>, you must meet specific criteria. Here are the key eligibility requirements:</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Ownership of a Qualifying Business</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>You must own a <strong>qualifying business</strong>. Whether you&rsquo;re applying solo or as part of a group (up to 5 members), you must:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Own at least <strong>10% of the business</strong>, and together with other applicants, hold more than <strong>50% of the total shares</strong>.</li>\r\n<li>Ensure that your business is <strong>incorporated in Canada</strong>, with a significant portion of its operations conducted in the country.</li>\r\n<li>Actively <strong>manage and operate the business</strong> from within Canada.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Getting Support from a Designated Organization</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Applicants must secure the backing of a <strong>designated organization</strong>. These are entities authorized by the Canadian government, which include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Angel investor groups</strong> &ndash; investing a minimum of <strong>$75,000</strong> into the business.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Venture capital funds</strong> &ndash; requiring a minimum investment of <strong>$200,000</strong>.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Business incubators</strong> &ndash; providing support without the need for direct investment.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Language Proficiency</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>All applicants must demonstrate proficiency in either <strong>English</strong> or <strong>French</strong>, with a minimum <strong>Canadian Language Benchmark (CLB) score of 5</strong> in each category.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Financial Requirements</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>To ensure you can settle comfortably, you must prove that you have enough funds to support yourself and your family. The amount varies depending on your family size but typically falls under <strong>$50,000</strong> for most applicants.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>The Application Process</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Initial Steps</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The first step in applying for the Start-up Visa is to gather all the required information about the program and your eligibility. Our team assists in identifying the right projects and partners necessary for your start-up.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>The Role of Designated Organizations</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Once a suitable project is identified, the business plan is presented to an <strong>Angel Investor (AI)</strong> or <strong>Venture Capitalist (VC)</strong>. Upon approval, they will commit <strong>$75,000</strong> or <strong>$200,000</strong> respectively to the project.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Submission of Application</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Once approved by the designated organization, a <strong>Letter of Support (LOS)</strong> is issued, which is a crucial document required for the permanent residency application. After obtaining the LOS, the final application, including <strong>biometric data, medical examinations</strong>, and <strong>police clearance certificates</strong>, is submitted for processing.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Processing Time</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>On average, it takes about <strong>30 to 36 months</strong> to process a Start-up Visa application, including the time needed for biometric data collection and medical examinations.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Legal and Professional Fees</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>For applicants using the <strong>Angel Investor</strong> and <strong>Venture Capital</strong> routes, the <strong>legal and professional fees</strong> typically range between <strong>USD 150,000 and USD 175,000</strong>. This fee includes a <strong>minimum equity shareholding</strong> of 10% in the start-up business.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Why Choose Canada for Business?</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Canada&rsquo;s Business-Friendly Environment</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Canada offers an incredibly welcoming environment for entrepreneurs. With its <strong>stable economy, robust infrastructure</strong>, and <strong>business-friendly policies</strong>, it&rsquo;s no wonder why many choose Canada for business expansion.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Opportunities for Innovation and Growth</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Canada\'s government places a high priority on <strong>innovation</strong> and <strong>research and development</strong> (R&amp;D). There are numerous <strong>tax credits and grants</strong> available to support start-ups, making it an ideal location for scaling innovative businesses.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>Conclusion</strong></h4>\r\n<p>The <a href=\"../news/Common-Mistakes-to-Avoid-When-Hiring-an-Immigration-Consultant\">Canada Startup Visa</a> Program is one of the best routes for entrepreneurs looking to settle in Canada while building innovative businesses. With its structured support system, investment opportunities, and strong economic environment, it is undoubtedly a program that opens doors to both business success and permanent residency.</p>\r\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>', 'uploads/1726118889_Eligibility Criteria for Canada Business Immigration.webp', 'Canada Business Immigration', '2024-09-12', '2024-09-12 05:28:09', '2024-09-12 05:37:11');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `metadata`, `news_detail`, `news_image`, `image_alt`, `news_date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(61, 'How to Score 65 Points for the Skilled Independent 189 Visa Tips and Insights', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Skilled Independent 189 Visa is an ideal route towards Australian permanent residency for skilled professionals.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"How to Score 65 Points for the Skilled Independent 189 Visa Tips and Insights\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Skilled Independent 189 Visa is an ideal route towards Australian permanent residency for skilled professionals.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1726207908_Australia%20Skilled%20Independent%20Visa%20(189).webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<p>Australia\'s Skilled Independent Visa, commonly referred to as Subclass 189, provides skilled professionals wishing to migrate permanently to Australia with an ideal opportunity. It does not require employer sponsorship, state nomination or family sponsorship - however qualifying requires scoring at least 65 points - we will help guide your application so as to maximize your chance of success and score as many points as possible in our guide.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>What is the Skilled Independent 189 Visa?</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Skilled Independent 189 Visa is a permanent residency visa designed for skilled professionals whose occupations appear on Australia\'s Skilled Occupation List (SOL). One major advantage is permanent residency status which opens doors to healthcare, education and citizenship options within Australia.</p>\r\n<h3><strong>How Does the Points-Based System Work?</strong></h3>\r\n<p>The points-based system is the cornerstone of the <a href=\"../service/australian-immigration-services/australian-skilled-worker/\">Australia Skilled Immigration Visa</a> application process. Points are awarded based on several factors, including age, English language proficiency, work experience, educational qualifications, and more. Each criterion has a maximum point value, and to apply for the 189 Visa, you must reach a minimum of 65 points.</p>\r\n<h3><strong>Key Criteria for Scoring 65 Points</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Here&rsquo;s a breakdown of the key areas where you can earn points:</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>1. Age (Maximum 30 points)</strong></span></h4>\r\n<p>Your age is a major factor in the points system:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> 18-24 years: 25 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> 25-32 years: 30 points (maximum points)</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> 33-39 years: 25 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>4)</strong> 40-44 years: 15 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>5)</strong> 45 years or older: 0 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>2. English Language Proficiency (Maximum 20 points)</strong></span></h4>\r\n<p>Proving your English proficiency through a recognized test like IELTS or PTE can give you a significant boost:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> Superior English: 20 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> Proficient English: 10 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> Competent English: 0 points (but still required to meet visa eligibility)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Aim for the highest score in your English language test to maximize your points. Superior English scores (IELTS 8 or above) can add 20 points, which is crucial in reaching the 65-point minimum.</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>3. Skilled Work Experience (Maximum 20 points)</strong></span></h4>\r\n<p>Your work experience as a skilled professional also plays a role. You can earn points based on the years of work both inside and outside Australia:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> 8 years or more (overseas experience): 15 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> 3-5 years (Australian experience): 10 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> 8 years or more (Australian experience): 20 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Ensure that your work experience is relevant to the occupation listed in the Skilled Occupation List (SOL) and that it&rsquo;s properly documented.</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>4. Educational Qualifications (Maximum 20 points)</strong></span></h4>\r\n<p>Your highest educational qualification can also contribute to your score:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> PhD: 20 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> Bachelor&rsquo;s or Master&rsquo;s degree: 15 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> Australian diploma or trade qualification: 10 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>4)</strong> Recognized qualification (relevant to occupation): 10 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>5. Partner Skills (Maximum 10 points)</strong></span></h4>\r\n<p>If your partner has skills and qualifications that meet certain criteria, you can earn additional points. The partner must be under 45, have competent English, and possess a positive skills assessment in a skilled occupation.</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>6. Additional Factors (Maximum 15 points)</strong></span></h4>\r\n<p>You can also earn points through additional factors such as:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> Study in regional Australia: 5 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> Professional year in Australia: 5 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> Credentialed community language: 5 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><strong>State Sponsorship and Regional Migration</strong></h3>\r\n<p>If you are willing to live in an Australian regional area, an application for a State Nominated Regional Visa (Subclass 491) could give you 15 extra points - making this visa ideal if your point count falls short of 65 needed for Subclass 189 Visa consideration.</p>\r\n<h3><strong>Tips to Create an Outstanding Expression of Interest (EOI)</strong></h3>\r\n<p>An Expression of Interest (EOI) is the initial step to applying for the Subclass 189 Visa. You should create an account on SkillSelect platform and submit your EOI there; be certain that all details submitted are complete as any discrepancies could delay or even deny your application.</p>\r\n<h3><strong>Skills Assessment Process</strong></h3>\r\n<p>To apply for the <a href=\"../news/Eligibility-Criteria-for-Canada-Business-Immigration\">189 Visa Australia</a>, you must have your skills assessed by the relevant assessing authority. This assessment is critical, as it determines whether your qualifications and work experience are recognized in Australia. Make sure to gather all necessary documents and meet the assessment criteria for your occupation.</p>\r\n<h3><strong>Common Mistakes to Avoid in the Application Process</strong></h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">1)</span> Inaccurate Documentation:</strong></span> Ensure that all documents submitted are accurate and up to date.</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">2)</span> Misunderstanding the Points System:</strong></span> Familiarize yourself with how points are allocated to maximize your chances.</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">3)</span> Skipping the Skills Assessment:</strong></span> A skills assessment is mandatory; skipping this step can lead to application rejection.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h4><strong>Conclusion</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Skilled Independent 189 Visa is an ideal route towards Australian permanent residency for skilled professionals. To increase your odds, aim for at least 65 points across key factors including age, English language proficiency, work experience and educational qualifications - following this guide\'s tips you will be well equipped to submit an effective application and begin their new adventure in Australia!</p>\r\n<h3>&nbsp;</h3>', 'uploads/1726207908_Australia Skilled Independent Visa (189).webp', 'Skilled Independent 189 Visa', '2024-09-13', '2024-09-13 06:11:48', '2024-09-13 06:21:21'),
(62, 'How to Score 65 Points for the Skilled Independent 190 Visa Simple Tips and Insights', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Secure 65 points on the Australia Skilled Immigration 190 Visa may seem difficult, but with planning and preparation it\'s achievable.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"How to Score 65 Points for the Skilled Independent 190 Visa Simple Tips and Insights\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Secure 65 points on the Australia Skilled Immigration 190 Visa may seem difficult, but with planning and preparation it\'s achievable.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1726288698_Australia%20Skilled%20Immigration%20190%20Visa.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<p>Skilled Nominated Visa (Subclass 190) is a permanent residency visa designed for <a href=\"../service/australian-immigration-services/australian-skilled-worker/\">Australia skilled worker</a> nominated by one or more Australian states and territories to live, work and study anywhere within Australia\'s boundaries. You can sponsor eligible family members to join you - with eligibility eventually leading up to citizenship status once meeting certain criteria is fulfilled.</p>\r\n<p>To qualify for a visa, applicants must first submit an Expression of Interest (EOI) through SkillSelect and receive approval by state/territorial governments to apply. A minimum score of 65 points must be attained to qualify, although many candidates attempt to get higher scores so as to increase their chance of selection.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>What is the Points-Based System for Subclass 190?</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Subclass 190 Visa evaluation system uses points-based evaluation criteria that take into account factors like age, English proficiency level, work experience and education to select individuals deemed capable of contributing positively to Australian economy. It aims to attract skilled individuals capable of strengthening the local economy.</p>\r\n<p>While a minimum score for applying is 65 points, higher scores increase your chance of receiving an invitation to apply for visa.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>Key Factors That Affect Your Points Score</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Understanding how points are allocated can help you better prepare your application. Here&rsquo;s a breakdown of the key factors:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Age</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> Younger applicants earn more points.</li>\r\n<li><strong>2) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">English proficiency</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> Higher language test scores can boost your points.</li>\r\n<li><strong>3) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Work experience</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> Both overseas and Australian work experience count.</li>\r\n<li><strong>4) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Education</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> Higher education degrees award more points.</li>\r\n<li><strong>5) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">State nomination</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> A nomination from a state or territory adds extra points.</li>\r\n<li><strong>6) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Partner skills</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> Your partner&rsquo;s qualifications can also contribute.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>How to Score Points for Age</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Age is one of the most significant factors in the points test. Points are awarded based on your age at the time of your EOI submission:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> 18&ndash;24 years: 25 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> 25&ndash;32 years: 30 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> 33&ndash;39 years: 25 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>4)</strong> 40&ndash;44 years: 15 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>5)</strong> 45 and above: 0 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>As you can see, applicants between 25 and 32 have the highest advantage when it comes to age points.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>English Language Proficiency</strong></h3>\r\n<p>To qualify for the Subclass 190 Visa, you must demonstrate a proficient level of English. Points are awarded based on your performance in recognized English language tests such as IELTS, TOEFL, or PTE.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Competent English</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> 0 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Proficient English</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> 10 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>3) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Superior English</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> 20 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Achieving a \"Proficient\" or \"Superior\" score can significantly boost your overall points.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>Work Experience: A Crucial Factor</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Work experience is another key component of the points system. Points are awarded based on the number of years you\'ve worked in a skilled occupation, both inside and outside Australia.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Outside Australia</strong>:</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> Less than 3 years: 0 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> 3&ndash;4 years: 5 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> 5&ndash;7 years: 10 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>4)</strong> 8+ years: 15 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Inside Australia</strong>:</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> Less than 1 year: 0 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> 1&ndash;2 years: 5 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> 3&ndash;4 years: 10 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>4)</strong> 5&ndash;7 years: 15 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>5)</strong> 8+ years: 20 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Combining both Australian and overseas work experience can maximize your score.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>Educational Qualifications and Points</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Educational qualifications also play a major role in your points score. Points are awarded based on the highest level of qualification you have:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">1)</span> Doctorate</strong>:</span> 20 points</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">2)</span> Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree</strong>:</span> 15 points</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">3)</span> Diploma or trade qualification</strong>:</span> 10 points</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">4)</span> Other qualifications</strong>:</span> 5 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Ensuring that your qualifications are recognized in Australia is crucial for claiming these points.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>State or Territory Nomination</strong></h2>\r\n<p>An endorsement by one of Australia\'s state or territory governments can increase your score by five points. Each state and territory maintains their own list of occupations in demand to qualify for visa consideration.</p>\r\n<p>Before applying, conduct research to find which state or territory best matches up with your skillset and career ambitions.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>Boosting Your Score with Partner Skills</strong></h3>\r\n<p>You can claim additional points if your partner meets certain criteria, such as being under the age of 45, having a suitable skills assessment, and demonstrating competent English proficiency. Partner points can be broken down as follows:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Partner has the necessary skills:</strong></span> 10 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Partner has competent English:</span> 5 points</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Partner does not meet criteria:</span> 0 points</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>If you are single, you can automatically claim 10 points.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>Other Factors That Can Increase Your Score</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Aside from the main criteria, there are a few additional ways to increase your points:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Community language skills</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> 5 points if you have proficiency in a language other than English.</li>\r\n<li><strong>2) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Study in regional Australia</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> 5 points if you completed 2 years of study in a regional area.</li>\r\n<li><strong>3) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Professional year in Australia</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> 5 points for completing a professional year in Australia.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>These extra points can help push your score higher if you\'re close to the minimum requirement.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>How to Maximize Your Points for the 190 Visa</strong></h3>\r\n<p>If you&rsquo;re just shy of the required 65 points, here are some tips to help boost your score:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">1) </span>Improve your English language score</strong>:</span> Retaking an English test can help you earn additional points.</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">2)</span> Gain more work experience</strong>:</span> Even a few additional months can make a difference.</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">3)</span> Consider state or territory nomination</strong>:</span> Research different regions that may align with your skills.</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">4)</span> Enhance your partner&rsquo;s qualifications</strong>:</span> Encourage your partner to take an English test or obtain a skills assessment.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>The Application Process for Subclass 190</strong></h3>\r\n<p>The application process for the Subclass 190 Visa consists of two main steps:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Submit an Expression of Interest (EOI)</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> You must lodge your EOI through SkillSelect. Your EOI will be ranked based on your points score.</li>\r\n<li><strong>2) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Receive an invitation</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> If your EOI is selected, you&rsquo;ll be invited to apply for the visa.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>It&rsquo;s important to ensure that your EOI is accurate and up-to-date to avoid any delays in the application process.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><strong>Common Pitfalls to Avoid in the 190 Visa Application</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Here are some common mistakes to watch out for:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">1)</span> Inaccurate claims in your EOI</strong>:</span> Double-check your information to avoid discrepancies.</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">2)</span> Not meeting the eligibility criteria</strong>:</span> Make sure you meet the minimum requirements for your nominated occupation.</li>\r\n<li><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">3)</span> Delays in obtaining documents</strong>:</span> Start gathering your documents early to prevent delays.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>What Happens After You Apply?</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Once your visa application has been submitted, processing times vary based on its specifics and may take anywhere between six to eight months for processing - during this time the Department of Home Affairs may also ask for further documents or information that needs to be supplied before approval can be given.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h4><strong>Conclusion</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Secure 65 points on the <a href=\"../news/How-to-Score-65-Points-for-the-Skilled-Independent-189-Visa-Tips-and-Insights\">Australia Skilled Immigration 190 Visa</a> may seem difficult, but with planning and preparation it\'s achievable. By placing emphasis on key factors like age, English proficiency, work experience and education you can maximize points and increase the chance that an invitation to apply will arrive for application. Each point counts and taking steps to improve it brings you one step closer towards making Australia home permanently.</p>', 'uploads/1726288698_Australia Skilled Immigration 190 Visa.webp', 'Skilled Independent 190 Visa', '2024-09-14', '2024-09-14 04:38:18', '2024-09-14 04:51:42'),
(63, 'Express Entry Draw in Canada Invited 1269 Healthcare Professionals on September 12 2024 for Professional Registration', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\"On September 12th 2024, Ontario Immigrant Nominee Program (OINP) issued 1,269 invitations through an Express Entry draw for Human Capital Priorities stream nominations.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Express Entry Draw in Canada Invited 1269 Healthcare Professionals on September 12 2024 for Professional Registration\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"On September 12th 2024, Ontario Immigrant Nominee Program (OINP) issued 1,269 invitations through an Express Entry draw for Human Capital Priorities stream nominations.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1726305532_Express%20Entry%20Draw%20in%20Canada.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<p>On September 12th 2024, Ontario Immigrant Nominee Program (OINP) issued 1,269 invitations through an <a href=\"../service/canadian-immigration-services/pnp-express-entry/\">Express Entry</a> draw for Human Capital Priorities stream nominations.</p>\r\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Healthcare Professionals Prioritize in the Latest Express Entry Draw</strong></h2>\r\n<p>OINP focused its recruitment efforts on Express Entry candidates seeking to settle in Ontario who held one of 43 healthcare-related primary vocations as their area of work experience.</p>\r\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Lowest CRS Score</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Candidates whose Express Entry profiles generated between September 12, 2023 and September 12, 2024 met these criteria and had a Comprehensive Ranking System score between 414-444 were invited to apply for provincial nomination through this draw.</p>\r\n<p>Invitees of provincial nomination have 45 days to respond.</p>\r\n<p>As soon as a provincial candidacy is approved by OINP, their CRS score increases from 600-1,044 points.</p>\r\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Are You Invited to an Express Entry Drawing?</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Here is the full list of occupations targeted in the Ontario Express Entry draw:</p>\r\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\">\r\n<div id=\"table_id_1\" class=\"table-responsive\">\r\n<table class=\"has-fixed-layout\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Occupation Name</strong></span></td>\r\n<td><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>NOC Code</strong></span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Managers in healthcare</td>\r\n<td>30010</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Specialists in clinical and laboratory medicine</td>\r\n<td>31100</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Specialists in surgery</td>\r\n<td>31101</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>General practitioners and family physicians</td>\r\n<td>31102</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Veterinarians</td>\r\n<td>31103</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Dentists</td>\r\n<td>31110</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Optometrists</td>\r\n<td>31111</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Audiologists and speech-language pathologists</td>\r\n<td>31112</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Pharmacists</td>\r\n<td>31120</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Dietitians and nutritionists</td>\r\n<td>31121</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Psychologists</td>\r\n<td>31200</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Chiropractors</td>\r\n<td>31201</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Physiotherapists</td>\r\n<td>31202</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Occupational therapists</td>\r\n<td>31203</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Kinesiologists and other professional occupations in therapy and assessment</td>\r\n<td>31204</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Other professional occupations in health diagnosing and treating</td>\r\n<td>31209</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Nursing coordinators and supervisors</td>\r\n<td>31300</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Registered nurses and registered psychiatric nurses</td>\r\n<td>31301</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Nurse practitioners</td>\r\n<td>31302</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Physician assistants, midwives, and allied health professionals</td>\r\n<td>31303</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Opticians</td>\r\n<td>32100</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Licensed practical nurses</td>\r\n<td>32101</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Paramedical occupations</td>\r\n<td>32102</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Respiratory therapists, clinical perfusionists, and cardiopulmonary technologists</td>\r\n<td>32103</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Animal health technologists and veterinary technicians</td>\r\n<td>32104</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Other technical occupations in therapy and assessment</td>\r\n<td>32109</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Denturists</td>\r\n<td>32110</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Dental hygienists and dental therapists</td>\r\n<td>32111</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Dental technologists and technicians</td>\r\n<td>32112</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Medical laboratory technologists</td>\r\n<td>32120</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Medical radiation technologists</td>\r\n<td>32121</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Medical sonographers</td>\r\n<td>32122</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Cardiology technologists and electrophysiological diagnostic technologists</td>\r\n<td>32123</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Pharmacy technicians</td>\r\n<td>32124</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Other medical technologists and technicians</td>\r\n<td>32129</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Traditional Chinese medicine practitioners and acupuncturists</td>\r\n<td>32200</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Massage therapists</td>\r\n<td>32201</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Other practitioners of natural healing</td>\r\n<td>32209</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Dental assistants and dental laboratory assistants</td>\r\n<td>33100</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Medical laboratory assistants and related technical occupations</td>\r\n<td>33101</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Nurse aides, orderlies, and patient service associates</td>\r\n<td>33102</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Pharmacy technical assistants and pharmacy assistants</td>\r\n<td>33103</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Other assisting occupations in support of health services</td>\r\n<td>33109</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</figure>\r\n<div class=\"apss-social-share apss-theme-5 clearfix \">\r\n<div class=\"apss-facebook apss-single-icon\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>', 'uploads/1726305532_Express Entry Draw in Canada.webp', 'Express Entry Draw in Canada', '2024-09-14', '2024-09-14 09:18:52', '2024-09-14 09:25:02'),
(64, 'How to Score 65 Points for the Skilled Independent 491 Visa Easy Advice and Helpful Insights', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Skilled Work Regional Visa 491 presents an ideal opportunity for skilled individuals looking to reside and work in Australia\'s regional areas, offering potential permanent residency status - making this visa an attractive long-term solution to improve the quality of life in Australia.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"How to Score 65 Points for the Skilled Independent 491 Visa Easy Advice and Helpful Insights\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Skilled Work Regional Visa 491 presents an ideal opportunity for skilled individuals looking to reside and work in Australia\'s regional areas, offering potential permanent residency status - making this visa an attractive long-term solution to improve the quality of life in Australia.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1726468919_Skilled%20Work%20Regional%20Visa%20491.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<p>Australia\'s regional areas offer skilled migrants unparalleled opportunities, especially through programs like the <a href=\"../service/australian-immigration-services/australian-skilled-worker/\">Australia Skilled Worker Program</a> and Skilled Work Regional Visa Subclass 491. This visa permits skilled individuals to reside, work, and study for up to five years within certain regional areas - making this visa more than merely temporary residency status; making this attractive proposition for skilled individuals who may wish to migrate here permanently.</p>\r\n<p>Are You Exploring Australia\'s Rural Landscapes, Contributing to Regional Communities or Looking to Settle Permanently in Australia? The 491 Visa is part of Australia Skilled Worker Program and could offer the means for you to do just this!</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Key Advantages of the Skilled Work Regional Visa</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Reside in Australia for 5 Years</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The 491 visa grants you five years\' of residency in Australia. Unlike other visas, however, this one focuses specifically on regional areas, giving you the chance to experience unique lifestyle, employment opportunities and culture of Australia\'s less urbanized regions.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Work and Study in Regional Australia</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Visa holders have the freedom and flexibility to live, work and study anywhere within Australia\'s regional areas - taking full advantage of Australia\'s advantages while increasing professional experience or continuing your studies in Australia.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Multiple Travel Opportunities</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>With a 491 visa, you are permitted to visit Australia as often as needed within any five year period, giving you freedom of travel between home country visits or leisure journeys without restrictions or limits on time spent within Australia\'s borders.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Pathway to Permanent Residency</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>After living in Australia for three years and meeting certain requirements, those holding 491 visas may apply for permanent residency visas - the Subclass 191. This offers significant incentives for long-term settlement.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Eligibility Requirements for the 491 Visa</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Nomination or Sponsorship</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>To apply for the 491 visa in Australia, applicants must either be nominated by an Australian state or territory government, or sponsored by an eligible relative residing within an approved regional area. This process ensures access to employment opportunities as well as community support services.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Skill Assessment</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Skill assessments are of vital importance in any application process. In order to show that your skills match those listed on Australia\'s Skilled Occupation List (SOL), and for review by an appropriate assessing authority. They\'ll determine if both qualifications and work experience meet Australian standards and will assess them against them accordingly.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Points Test (Score 65 or Above)</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Australia\'s points-based immigration system requires applicants for the 491 visa to score at least 65 points on its points scale in order to be considered. Points may be awarded depending on factors like age, English proficiency level, qualifications obtained and work experience - the higher your score the greater are your chances of receiving an invitation to submit an application.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Age Requirement (Under 45 Years)</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>At the time of receiving an invitation, those aged 45 or under must ensure skilled migrants will make long-term contributions to our workforce.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>English Proficiency</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Demonstrating Competent English requires passing recognized English exams such as IELTS, PTE or TOEFL. Proficiency in English is crucial to communicating within Australia\'s workplace environment and integration.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Health and Character Requirements</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>All applicants to Australia must satisfy Australia\'s health and character requirements, which involves passing medical examinations and police checks in order to meet Australia\'s minimum health standards while remaining criminal record free.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>What is the 491 Visa?</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Skilled Work Regional Visa 491 allows skilled workers and their immediate families to live, work and study in regional Australia for up to five years, providing a pathway towards permanent residency if the eligibility requirements are fulfilled.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Nomination or Sponsorship for the Visa</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>To be eligible to apply for the 491 visa, either nominated by your state or territory government or sponsored by an eligible relative living within one of several designated regional areas is needed to make your application. This ensures that skilled migrants receive appropriate support while being fully integrated into society.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Understanding the Points Test</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Points for the 491 visa are calculated based on multiple factors, including:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> Age</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> English language proficiency</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> Skilled work experience (in Australia or overseas)</li>\r\n<li><strong>4)</strong> Educational qualifications</li>\r\n<li><strong>5)</strong> Nomination/sponsorship points</li>\r\n<li><strong>6)</strong> Partner skills</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The goal is to achieve a minimum score of 65 points, which is necessary to receive an invitation to apply for the visa.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<p><em><strong>Conclusion</strong></em></p>\r\n<p><a href=\"../news/How-to-Score-65-Points-for-the-Skilled-Independent-190-Visa-Simple-Tips-and-Insights\">Skilled Work Regional Visa 491</a> presents an ideal opportunity for skilled individuals looking to reside and work in Australia\'s regional areas, offering potential permanent residency status - making this visa an attractive long-term solution to improve the quality of life in Australia.</p>', 'uploads/1726468919_Skilled Work Regional Visa 491.webp', 'Skilled Independent 491 Visa', '2024-09-16', '2024-09-16 06:41:59', '2024-09-16 06:53:47');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `metadata`, `news_detail`, `news_image`, `image_alt`, `news_date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(65, 'Your Ultimate Guide to PNP Express Entry A Step Toward Canadian Immigration', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\"No matter how you apply to Canada for permanent residency - Express Entry or Provincial Nominee Program (PNP), both options provide excellent chances. Each has unique advantages that could increase the success rate; using both programs together could further maximize success rates.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Your Ultimate Guide to PNP Express Entry A Step Toward Canadian Immigration\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"No matter how you apply to Canada for permanent residency - Express Entry or Provincial Nominee Program (PNP), both options provide excellent chances. Each has unique advantages that could increase the success rate; using both programs together could further maximize success rates.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1726635651_Your%20Ultimate%20Guide%20to%20PNP%20Express%20Entry%20A%20Step%20Toward%20Canadian%20Immigration.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<h2><strong>What is PNP Express Entry?</strong></h2>\r\n<p><a href=\"../service/canadian-immigration-services/pnp-express-entry/\">PNP Express Entry</a> is an innovative Canadian immigration system combining two powerful programs - Provincial Nominee Program (PNP) and Express Entry - in order to attract skilled workers into Canada. While Express Entry serves as the main application platform worldwide, provinces may nominate specific individuals through PNP for immigration to meet local needs.</p>\r\n<p>Canada benefits from this combination by recruiting and retaining talent with skills needed in local economies for long-term economic development.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Understanding Express Entry</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Express Entry is Canada\'s federal immigration management system for processing applications for permanent residency. This application process encompasses three streams:</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Federal Skilled Worker Program (FSWP)</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The Federal Skilled Worker Program recognizes individuals with experience, education and skills that are in high demand in Canada. Points are awarded based on age, education level, work experience and language abilities.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Federal Skilled Trades Program (FSTP)</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The Federal Skilled Trades Program focuses on people with skills in industries like construction, electrical work and plumbing. To be considered eligible for this grant program, applicants should possess at least two years full-time work experience within these trades.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Canadian Experience Class (CEC)</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The Canadian Experience Class is tailored for individuals who have worked or studied in Canada for at least one year and is designed to assist temporary workers or students who have gained experience there to become permanent residents of this nation.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Provincial Nominee Program (PNP) Overview</strong></h2>\r\n<p>PNP (Provincial Nominee Program) allows Canadian provinces and territories to nominate people looking to settle in specific provinces based on local labor market needs, with nomination resulting in 600 additional points being added onto your Comprehensive Ranking System score and increasing your chance of permanent residency application acceptance.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>How Express Entry and PNP Work Together</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Express Entry and PNP work together by allowing provinces to select skilled workers from the Express Entry pool. When a candidate gets nominated by a province, they receive extra points in the CRS system. This boosts their chance of getting an Invitation to Apply (ITA) for permanent residency.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>How to Check Your Eligibility for Express Entry</strong></h2>\r\n<p>To apply for Express Entry, you must first check your eligibility. The basic requirements include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> Age (preferably between 25 to 38 years old)</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> Work experience (at least one year in a skilled job)</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> Education (equivalent to a Canadian diploma or degree)</li>\r\n<li><strong>4)</strong> Language skills (a minimum of 6 bands in IELTS)</li>\r\n<li><strong>5)</strong> Settlement funds (to support yourself and your family in Canada)</li>\r\n<li><strong>6)</strong> Good health and a police clearance certificate</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Steps to Apply for Express Entry</strong></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Create an Express Entry profile</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> Include your education, work experience, language test results, and other details.</li>\r\n<li><strong>2) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Receive a CRS score</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> Based on the information you provide, you\'ll receive a score out of 1,200.</li>\r\n<li><strong>3) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Submit your profile</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> You will enter the Express Entry pool, where the federal government and provinces can select you for immigration.</li>\r\n<li><strong>4) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Receive an ITA</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> If your CRS score is high enough, you may receive an ITA for permanent residency.</li>\r\n<li><strong>5) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Submit your application</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> After receiving an ITA, you have 60 days to submit your application for permanent residency.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Benefits of Applying Through Express Entry</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Applying through Express Entry offers several benefits:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Faster processing times</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> Most applications are processed within six months.</li>\r\n<li><strong>2) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Higher chances of employment</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> You can get a job offer even before moving to Canada.</li>\r\n<li><strong>3) <span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">Permanent residency for you and your family</span></strong><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\">:</span> Upon approval, you and your family can live and work anywhere in Canada.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Introduction to Provincial Nominee Programs (PNPs)</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Every Canadian province and territory (except Quebec) has its own PNP, designed to address specific labor market needs. Each province can select individuals from the Express Entry pool and nominate them for immigration.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Popular PNP Programs by Province</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Saskatchewan Immigrant Nominee Program (SINP)</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Saskatchewan is known for its beautiful landscapes and affordable lifestyle. The <strong>SINP</strong> allows the province to nominate skilled workers who can fill local job shortages.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Ontario Immigration Nominee Program (OINP)</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Ontario, home to the bustling city of Toronto, attracts many immigrants. The <strong>OINP</strong> is for individuals with the skills and experience that are in high demand in the province.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Manitoba Immigration Nominee Program</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Manitoba&rsquo;s economy thrives on agriculture and natural resources. The <strong>Manitoba PNP</strong> nominates individuals with strong ties to the province or those who meet its labor needs.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Alberta Provincial Nominee Program (AINP)</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Alberta&rsquo;s oil and gas industry is booming, and the <strong>AINP</strong> focuses on selecting skilled workers who can contribute to this and other growing industries.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Quebec Skilled Worker Program</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Although Quebec does not participate in the federal PNP system, it has its own skilled worker program. Quebec focuses on individuals who can integrate into the province\'s unique French-speaking culture.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Why PNP is Important for Local Labor Markets</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Provincial Nominee Program helps provinces address specific skill shortages. Whether it&rsquo;s engineers for Alberta&rsquo;s oil fields or healthcare workers in Manitoba, PNP allows regions to invite the right people to keep their local economies growing.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>How PNP Help You Boost Your Express Entry Score</strong></h2>\r\n<p>If you&rsquo;re nominated by a province through a PNP, you get an additional 600 points on your CRS score. This is a major boost and almost guarantees an ITA for permanent residency.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>How to Get Nominated by a Province</strong></h2>\r\n<p>To get nominated, you&rsquo;ll need to:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> Create an Express Entry profile.</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> Research the provinces and check their specific requirements.</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> Submit an Expression of Interest (EOI) to the province you&rsquo;re interested in.</li>\r\n<li><strong>4)</strong> If selected, you&rsquo;ll be invited to apply for nomination.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>How to Increase Your Chances of Success</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Here are some tips to improve your chances of getting selected for Express Entry or PNP:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>1)</strong> Improve your language scores.</li>\r\n<li><strong>2)</strong> Gain more work experience.</li>\r\n<li><strong>3)</strong> Apply to provinces that have a high demand for your skills.</li>\r\n<li><strong>4)</strong> Stay updated on changes to immigration rules.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Final Thoughts on Canadian Immigration Pathways</strong></h2>\r\n<p>No matter how you apply to <a href=\"../news/How-to-Score-65-Points-for-the-Skilled-Independent-491-Visa-Easy-Advice-and-Helpful-Insights\">Canada</a> for permanent residency - Express Entry or Provincial Nominee Program (PNP), both options provide excellent chances. Each has unique advantages that could increase the success rate; using both programs together could further maximize success rates.</p>', 'uploads/1726635651_Your Ultimate Guide to PNP Express Entry A Step Toward Canadian Immigration.webp', 'PNP Express Entry', '2024-09-18', '2024-09-18 05:00:51', '2024-09-18 05:04:34'),
(66, 'Canada Ready to Improve Immigration System Marc Miller Key Announcement', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Canada is set to announce major immigration reforms today, focusing on reducing fraud and protecting temporary residents. Stay tuned for live updates!\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Canada Ready to Improve Immigration System Marc Miller Key Announcement\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Canada is set to announce major immigration reforms today, focusing on reducing fraud and protecting temporary residents. Stay tuned for live updates!\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1726725249_Immigration%20System%20Marc%20Miller%20Key%20Announcement.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<p>Canada is gearing up for an important announcement regarding its immigration system. As Canada becomes a more attractive destination for international students, skilled professionals, and temporary workers, the demand for an efficient, fair immigration system has never been greater. On September 18th two prominent Canadian ministers are set to release new measures which could shape immigration in Canada in years to come.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Overview of Canada\'s Immigration System</strong></h2>\r\n<p><a href=\"../\">Canadian immigration</a> plays an integral part in shaping its economy and culture, attracting migrants from across the globe who come seeking greater job opportunities, education opportunities and an improved quality of life. Immigration plays an indispensable role not just for Canada\'s growth but also its diversity and global connections.</p>\r\n<h3><strong>Importance of Immigration to Canada\'s Economy and Society</strong></h3>\r\n<p>From filling labor gaps to bringing in new ideas and cultures, immigrants are key to Canada&rsquo;s progress. International students enrich the academic landscape, while skilled workers help boost the economy. However, with the system under increasing strain, the government recognizes that improvements must be made to ensure fairness and efficiency.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Upcoming Announcement: Key Figures Involved</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Two ministers will be at the forefront of this significant announcement.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Marc Miller&rsquo;s Role as Minister of Immigration</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>As Canada\'s Minister of Immigration, Marc Miller is charged with setting policies determining who may enter and remain in Canada. His main priority has been improving both temporary and permanent residency programs.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Randy Boissonnault&rsquo;s Contribution to Workforce Development</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Randy Boissonnault oversees employment and workforce development. His participation in this announcement is essential as it assists with creating equal opportunities for Canadians and immigrants while making sure our nation benefits from global talent.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Challenges Facing Canada\'s Immigration System</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Canada&rsquo;s immigration system, while robust, is facing growing challenges.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Rising Demand for Immigration</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>With more people wanting to move to Canada for education and work, the government is under pressure to process applications quickly while maintaining security and fairness.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Problems of Fraud and Abuse</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Unfortunately, there have been cases of immigration fraud and the mistreatment of temporary foreign workers. Addressing these issues is crucial for maintaining the credibility of Canada&rsquo;s immigration system.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>What to Expect from the Announcement</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Though we won&rsquo;t know the full details until the official announcement, there are some expected focus areas.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Potential Focus Areas</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The government is expected to focus on improving temporary resident programs, protecting immigrants from exploitation, and ensuring smoother paths to permanent residency.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Temporary Resident Programs for Students and Workers</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Both international students and temporary workers contribute significantly to Canada&rsquo;s economy. The new policies could enhance protections for these groups, making it easier for them to stay long-term.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Enhancing Pathways to Permanent Residency</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Clearer Routes for International Students</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Many international students hope to remain in Canada after their studies. The announcement could include clearer pathways to permanent residency, making the process more straightforward for students who wish to build their futures in Canada.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Securing Foreign Workers&rsquo; Rights</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Temporary foreign workers need their rights and safety protected as a priority, especially since their work in industries such as agriculture and construction is essential. Therefore, the government should take appropriate action against any attempts by employers or others to exploit temporary workers.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Fighting Immigration Fraud</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Strengthening Monitoring Systems</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Immigration fraud is a serious issue. The government may announce tougher regulations and more robust monitoring systems to detect and prevent fraud.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Tougher Penalties for Exploitation</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>In cases where temporary workers are exploited, harsher penalties may be introduced to hold perpetrators accountable.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Background Checks for Visa Applicants</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Responding to Security Concerns</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Recent reports of individuals with questionable backgrounds entering Canada have raised security concerns. It&rsquo;s likely that the announcement will include stricter background checks to prevent such incidents.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Stricter Screening Measures</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Tighter visa screening processes could be introduced to ensure that individuals entering Canada do not pose any security risks.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Labour Market Impact Assessment (LMIA) Reforms</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Preventing LMIA Fraud</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Labour Market Impact Assessments (LMIAs) are required to hire temporary foreign workers. However, there have been instances of fraud in this area, and the government is expected to address this issue head-on.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>New Policies to Curb Illegal Practices</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The new announcement could include more stringent policies to prevent illegal practices and protect both Canadian and foreign workers.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>How Canada is Preparing for the Future</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Keeping Immigration Safe and Transparent</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The Canadian government is committed to ensuring that the immigration system remains transparent and safe. This includes preventing abuse and maintaining fairness for all applicants.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Long-Term Impact on the Economy</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>By improving the immigration system, Canada can attract the best global talent, contributing to long-term economic growth.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Impact on International Students</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Ensuring Safety and Security</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>New measures may be introduced to ensure that international students studying in Canada&nbsp;are safe from exploitation and have access to resources that help them succeed.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Easing the Transition to Permanent Residency</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>For students who wish to remain in Canada, the government could make the transition from temporary residency to permanent status easier and more streamlined.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Support for Temporary Foreign Workers</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Protection Against Exploitation</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Temporary foreign workers are often vulnerable to abuse. The upcoming announcement may include stronger protections and support systems to ensure their rights are respected.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Creating Fair Employment Opportunities</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>New policies could ensure that these workers are given fair employment opportunities, contributing to Canada&rsquo;s workforce in a meaningful way.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>The Government&rsquo;s Commitment to a Just System</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Ensuring Fair Treatment for All Immigrants</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>The government is dedicated to making sure that all immigrants, whether temporary or permanent, are treated fairly and respectfully throughout their time in Canada.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Upholding the Integrity of the Immigration System</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>By addressing issues like fraud and exploitation, the government aims to uphold the integrity of Canada&rsquo;s immigration system, ensuring it remains strong and just.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h2><strong>Looking Ahead: What the Changes Mean</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Strengthening Canada&rsquo;s Position Globally</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>As Canada continues to be a top destination for immigrants, these changes will likely help the country maintain its global reputation for fairness and opportunity.</p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Maintaining Openness While Ensuring Safety</strong></span></h3>\r\n<p>Canada will remain open to immigrants, but with improved systems that ensure safety and prevent fraud. This balance is key to a successful and thriving immigration policy.</p>\r\n<hr>\r\n<h4><em><strong>Conclusion</strong></em></h4>\r\n<p>Canada stands on the verge of an important turning point in its immigration journey. With today\'s announcement by its government, major steps will be taken towards improving its system - by eliminating fraud, protecting temporary resident rights, and assuring fair treatment, <a href=\"https://www.canada.ca/en.html\">Canada</a> lays down a foundation that ensures immigration remains an integral component of national growth. Follow us as we bring updates as the announcement unfolds live!</p>', 'uploads/1726725249_Immigration System Marc Miller Key Announcement.webp', 'Improve Immigration System Marc Miller', '2024-09-19', '2024-09-19 05:54:09', '2024-09-19 05:55:30'),
(67, 'Canada Invites 1424 Candidates for Permanent Residency in Latest Express Entry Draw on September 19 2024', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Ontario Immigrant Nominee Program (OINP) issued 1,424 invites on September 19th as a part of its provincial nomination draw through the Express Entry Human Capital Priorities stream.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Canada Invites 1424 Candidates for Permanent Residency in Latest Express Entry Draw on September 19 2024\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Ontario Immigrant Nominee Program (OINP) issued 1,424 invites on September 19th as a part of its provincial nomination draw through the Express Entry Human Capital Priorities stream.\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1726897640_Canada%20Invites%201424%20Candidates%20for%20Permanent%20Residency%20in%20Latest%20Express%20Entry%20Draw%20on%20September%2019%202024.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col flex-grow AIPRM__conversation__response\">\r\n<div class=\"min-h-[20px] text-message flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 whitespace-normal break-words [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"09ba7b5d-87a2-46a4-86a8-55235f005f71\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]\">\r\n<div class=\"markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark\">\r\n<p>Ontario Immigrant Nominee Program (OINP) issued 1,424 invites on September 19th as a part of its provincial nomination draw through the Express Entry Human Capital Priorities stream.</p>\r\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Overview Express Entry Draw September 19-2024</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Candidates with Comprehensive Ranking System (CRS) scores between 505 and 528 who submitted <a href=\"../service/canadian-immigration-services/pnp-express-entry/\">Express Entry</a> profiles between September 19, 2023, and September 19, 2024 have been invited to apply for provincial nomination in the Ontario Immigrant Nominee Program\'s most recent draw.</p>\r\n<p>OINP prioritizes Express Entry applicants who possess work experience in one of 103 priority occupations and want to reside in Ontario as priority applicants for OINP consideration.</p>\r\n<p>Candidates selected for provincial nomination receive their invitation within 45 days and have 45 days to respond.</p>\r\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>List of Occupations Invited in Express Entry Draw</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Here is the following list of invited occupations with their associated NOC codes:</p>\r\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\">\r\n<div id=\"table_id_1\" class=\"table-responsive\">\r\n<table class=\"has-fixed-layout\" style=\"width: 100.052%; height: 3784.27px;\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 58.5625px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>Occupation</strong></span></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\"><span style=\"color: #bf8f59;\"><strong>NOC Code</strong></span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>1)</strong> Senior Managers: Construction, Transportation, Production and Utilities</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">00015</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>2)</strong> Accounting Technicians and Bookkeepers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12200</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>3)</strong> Property Administrators</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">13101</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>4)</strong> Payroll Administrators</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">13102</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>5)</strong> Financial Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">10010</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>6)</strong> Human Resources Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">10011</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>7)</strong> Advertising, Marketing and Public Relations Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">10022</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>8)</strong> Financial Auditors and Accountants</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">11100</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>9)</strong> Human Resources Professionals</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">11200</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>10)</strong> Professional Occupations in Advertising, Marketing and Public Relations</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">11202</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>11)</strong> Executive Assistants</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12100</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>12)</strong> Procurement and Purchasing Agents and Officers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12102</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>13)</strong> Civil Engineers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">21300</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>14)</strong> Mechanical Engineers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">21301</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>15)</strong> Electrical and Electronics Engineers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">21310</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>16)</strong> Drafting Technologists and Technicians</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">22212</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>17)</strong> Construction Inspectors</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">22233</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>18)</strong> Construction Estimators</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">22303</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>19)</strong> Electrical and Electronics Engineering Technologists and Technicians</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">22310</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>20)</strong> Electronic Service Technicians (Household and Business Equipment)</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">22311</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>21)</strong> Interior Designers and Interior Decorators</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">52121</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>22)</strong> Corporate Sales Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">60010</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>23)</strong> Purchasing Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">10012</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>24)</strong> Insurance, Real Estate and Financial Brokerage Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">10020</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>25)</strong> Banking, Credit and Other Investment Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">10021</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>26)</strong> Other Business Services Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">10029</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>27)</strong> Financial and Investment Analysts</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">11101</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>28)</strong> Securities Agents, Investment Dealers and Brokers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">11103</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>29)</strong> Professional Occupations in Business Management Consulting</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">11201</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>30)</strong> Supervisors, General Office and Administrative Support Workers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12010</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>31)</strong> Supervisors, Finance and Insurance Office Workers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12011</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>32)</strong> Supervisors, Library, Correspondence and Related Information Workers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12012</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>33)</strong> Human Resources and Recruitment Officers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12101</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>34)</strong> Conference and Event Planners</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12103</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>35)</strong> Court Reporters, Medical Transcriptionists and Related Occupations</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12110</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>36)</strong> Health Information Management Occupations</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12111</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>37)</strong> Records Management Technicians</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12112</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>38)</strong> Statistical Officers and Related Research Support Occupations</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12113</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>39)</strong> Insurance Adjusters and Claims Examiners</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12201</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>40)</strong> Insurance Underwriters</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12202</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>41)</strong> Assessors, Valuators and Appraisers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">12203</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>42)</strong> Legal Administrative Assistants</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">13111</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>43)</strong> Medical Administrative Assistants</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">13112</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>44)</strong> Customs, Ship, and Other Brokers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">13200</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>45)</strong> Engineering Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">20010</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>46)</strong> Architecture and Science Managers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">20011</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>47)</strong> Geoscientists and Oceanographers</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">21102</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>48)</strong> Forestry Professionals</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">21111</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>49)</strong> Architects</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">21200</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>50)</strong> Landscape Architects</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">21201</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>51)</strong> Urban and Land Use Planners</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">21202</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 36.1719px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 87.1158%;\"><strong>52)</strong> Land Surveyors</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.45626%;\">21203</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"hei