</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-39\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Elevator constructors and mechanics</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72406</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-40\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Automotive service technicians, truck and bus mechanics, and mechanical repairers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72410</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-41\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Auto body collision, refinishing, and glass technicians and damage repair estimators</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72411</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-42\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Oil and solid fuel heating mechanics</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72420</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-43\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Appliance servicers and repairers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72421</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-44\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Electrical Mechanics</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72422</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-45\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Motorcycle, all-terrain vehicle, and other related mechanics</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72423</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-46\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Other small engine and small equipment repairers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72429</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-47\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Crane operators</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72500</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-48\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Water well drillers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72501</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-49\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Air pilots, flight engineers, and flying instructors</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72600</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-50\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Air traffic controllers and related occupations</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72601</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-51\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Deck officers, water transport</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72602</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-52\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Engineer officers, water transport</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72603</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-53\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Railway traffic controllers and marine traffic regulators</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72604</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-54\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Other technical trades and related occupations</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">72999</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤ </span>NOC group 82 - Supervisors in Natural Resources, Agriculture, and Related Production</strong></h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"post-table\">\r\n<table id=\"tablepress-506-no-3\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-506\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\r\n<th class=\"column-1\">Occupation Title</th>\r\n<th class=\"column-2\">NOC Code</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody class=\"row-striping row-hover\">\r\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Supervisors, logging and forestry</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">82010</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-3\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Supervisors, mining and quarrying</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">82020</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-4\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Contractors and supervisors, oil and gas drilling and services</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">82021</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-5\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Agricultural service contractors and farm supervisors</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">82030</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-6\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Contractors and supervisors, landscaping, grounds maintenance, and horticulture services</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">82031</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">TEER 3 jobs still eligible for a family OWP</span></strong></h2>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤ </span>NOC group 33 - Assisting Occupations in Support of Health Services</strong></h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"post-table\">\r\n<table id=\"tablepress-507-no-3\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-507\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\r\n<th class=\"column-1\">Occupation Title</th>\r\n<th class=\"column-2\">NOC Code</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody class=\"row-striping row-hover\">\r\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Dental assistants and dental laboratory assistants</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">33100</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-3\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Medical laboratory assistants and related technical occupations</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">33101</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-4\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Nurse aides, orderlies and patient service associates</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">33102</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-5\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Pharmacy technical assistants and pharmacy assistants</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">33103</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-6\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Other assisting occupations in support of health services</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">33109</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤ </span>NOC group 43 - Assisting Occupations in Education and in Legal and Public Protection</strong></h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"post-table\">\r\n<table id=\"tablepress-508-no-3\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-508\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\r\n<th class=\"column-1\">Occupation Title</th>\r\n<th class=\"column-2\">NOC Code</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody class=\"row-striping row-hover\">\r\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Elementary and secondary school teacher assistants</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">43100</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-3\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Operations Members of the Canadian Armed Forces</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">43204</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤ </span>NOC group 53 - Occupations in Art, Culture, and Sport</strong></h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"post-table\">\r\n<table id=\"tablepress-509-no-3\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-509\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\r\n<th class=\"column-1\">Occupation Title</th>\r\n<th class=\"column-2\">NOC Code</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody class=\"row-striping row-hover\">\r\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Athletes</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">53200</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-3\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Coaches</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">53201</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤ </span>NOC Group 73 - General Trades</strong></h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"post-table\">\r\n<table id=\"tablepress-510-no-3\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-510\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\r\n<th class=\"column-1\">Occupation Title</th>\r\n<th class=\"column-2\">NOC Code</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody class=\"row-striping row-hover\">\r\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Concrete finishers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73100</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-3\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Tile setters</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73101</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-4\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Plasterers, drywall installers and finishers, and lathers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73102</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-5\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Roofers and shinglers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73110</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-6\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Glaziers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73111</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-7\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Painters and decorators (except interior decorators</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73112</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-8\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Floor covering installers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73113</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-9\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Residential and commercial installers and servicers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73200</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-10\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>General building maintenance workers and building superintendents</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73201</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-11\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Pest controllers and fumigators</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73202</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-12\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Other repairers and servicers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73209</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-13\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Transport truck drivers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73300</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-14\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Bus drivers, subway operators, and other transit operators</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73301</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-15\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Railway and yard locomotive engineers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73310</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-16\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Railway conductors and brakemen/women</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73311</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-17\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Heavy equipment operators</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73400</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-18\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Printing press operators</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73401</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-19\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Drillers and blasters - surface mining, quarrying, and construction</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">73402</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<div id=\"cicnewsads-c9b6f05db8a90c1fc4e53c7c10608544\" class=\"cicnewsads-c9b6f05db8a90c1fc4e53c7c10608544 cicnewsads-in-article-2\">\r\n<div id=\"cicnewsads-1494046325\" class=\"cicnewsads-in-article-2\">\r\n<div id=\"gpt-ad-4487912739570-0\" data-google-query-id=\"CI72nfGAi4sDFU8kBgAd2lEuag\">\r\n<div id=\"google_ads_iframe_/22646143967/cicnews.com/cicnews_in_article_3__container__\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤ </span>NOC group 83 - Occupations in Natural Resources and Related Production</strong></h3>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"post-table\">\r\n<table id=\"tablepress-511-no-3\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-511\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\r\n<th class=\"column-1\">Occupation Title</th>\r\n<th class=\"column-2\">NOC Code</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody class=\"row-striping row-hover\">\r\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Underground production and development miners</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">83100</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-3\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Oil and gas well drillers, servicers, testers, and related workers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">83101</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-4\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Logging machinery operators</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">83110</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-5\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Fishing masters and officers</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">83120</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr class=\"row-6\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\"><strong>&bull; </strong>Fishermen/women</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">83121</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2><strong>How to find your occupation&rsquo;s NOC code</strong></h2>\r\n<p>The job title associated with your <a href=\"https://www.cicnews.com/2025/01/these-are-the-teer-2-and-3-jobs-that-can-still-get-your-spouse-a-family-open-work-permit-0150760.html\">occupation&rsquo;s NOC code</a> may not match the job title given by your employer. For the purposes of the NOC, what matters is which duties and responsibilities you performed for a given role (regardless of what your title was).</p>\r\n<p>To determine your NOC code, compare the main duties listed in the NOC to the duties you performed in your role. For most immigration purposes, you must have performed all the duties in the lead statement of the NOC, and at least 51% of the main duties.</p>\r\n<p>For more details on the&nbsp;<strong>TEER levels</strong> and Canada&rsquo;s NOC system, visit the official immigration webpage.</p>\r\n<h3><strong>How to Apply for a Spousal Open Work Permit (SOWP) with Lalani &amp; Associates</strong></h3>\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col flex-grow AIPRM__conversation__response\">\r\n<div class=\"min-h-8 text-message flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 whitespace-normal break-words text-start [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"a49bc8a8-8115-4786-8804-079e780957a1\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-4o-mini\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]\">\r\n<div class=\"markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert dark\">\r\n<p>At Lalani &amp; Associates, we provide full support throughout the entire immigration process. From the moment you contact us, we take the stress out of applying for your visa. Here&rsquo;s what we do for you:</p>\r\n<p><strong>▲ <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Expert Guidance</span></strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">:</span> Our team of experienced immigration consultants and lawyers will guide you through every step of the visa application process. We ensure that all your documents are in order and that your application meets the requirements.</p>\r\n<p><strong>▲ <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Comprehensive Documentation</span></strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">:</span> We help you gather and organize all the necessary paperwork, including proof of relationship, employment, and eligibility for the visa you are applying for.</p>\r\n<p><strong>▲ <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Eligibility Assessment</span></strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">:</span> We evaluate your eligibility for the visa and provide personalized recommendations based on your specific situation. Whether you\'re applying for a work permit, spousal open work permit, or any other immigration program, we ensure you have the best chance of success.</p>\r\n<p><strong>▲ <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Legal Representation</span></strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">:</span> Our lawyers handle all legal matters, ensuring that your application is submitted correctly and on time. We also address any legal issues that may arise throughout the process, so you don&rsquo;t have to worry.</p>\r\n<p><strong>▲ <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Application Submission</span></strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">:</span> Once your documents are prepared, we submit your application to the appropriate authorities. We take care of all the details to ensure everything is processed smoothly.</p>\r\n<p><strong>▲ <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Regular Updates</span></strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">:</span> We keep you informed throughout the entire process, providing updates on the status of your application and addressing any questions or concerns you may have.</p>\r\n<p><strong>▲ <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Visa Approval</span></strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">:</span> With our expertise and dedication, we work hard to secure your visa. Once your application is approved, we will ensure you receive your visa without any hassle.</p>\r\n<p>At Lalani &amp; Associates, we are committed to making your immigration process as easy and successful as possible. With our team working for you, you can be confident that your visa application is in the best hands. Don&rsquo;t worry &ndash; our lawyers are here to work for you!</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2><strong>Background on today&rsquo;s change</strong></h2>\r\n<p>Today&rsquo;s measures are part of a wider suite of initiatives that the Canadian government has undertaken to&nbsp;reduce the temporary resident&nbsp;(study or work permit holder) population in Canada.</p>\r\n<p>The changes to SOWP eligibility for spouses of students and foreign workers in effect today were first announced in September of 2024.</p>\r\n<p>At a press conference on September 18 of that year, Immigration Minister Marc Miller said that the government would be&nbsp;<a>limiting the availability of SOWPs to spouses of foreign workers</a>&nbsp;working in highly skilled and/or in-demand occupations. At the time the minister provided only a high-level description of which occupations would provide for SOWP eligibility.</p>\r\n<p>In addition, at the same press conference, Miller also announced his intention to limit the availability of SOWPs to spouses of international students enrolled in</p>\r\n<p>⦿ Doctoral programs;<br>⦿ Master\'s programs of at least 16 months in duration Study at the master\'s level; or<br>⦿ One of the following professional degree programs:</p>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; </strong>Doctor of Dental Surgery (DDS, DMD).<br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; </strong>Bachelor of Law or Juris Doctor (LLB, JD, BCL).<br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; </strong>Doctor of Medicine (MD).<br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; </strong>Doctor of Optometry (OD).<br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; </strong>Pharmacy (PharmD, BS, BSc, BPharm).<br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; </strong>Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM).<br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; </strong>Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BScN, BSN, BNSc).<br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; </strong>Bachelor of Education (B. Ed.).<br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; </strong>Bachelor of Engineering (B. Eng., BE, BASc).</p>\r\n<p>Miller said that the government expected that the above changes would result in the issuance of 150,000 fewer SOWPs over the next three years.</p>\r\n<p>Further to these changes, IRCC has also implemented targets for admission of net new work permit holders under the International Mobility Program (IMP) - under which SOWPs are issued - within the annual Immigration Levels Plan.&nbsp;The following table breaks down IRCC&rsquo;s planned total admissions of net new IMP work permit holders from 2025 to 2027:</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<div class=\"post-table\">\r\n<table id=\"tablepress-512-no-3\" class=\"tablepress tablepress-id-512\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr class=\"row-1\">\r\n<th class=\"column-1\">Year</th>\r\n<th class=\"column-2\">2025</th>\r\n<th class=\"column-3\">2026</th>\r\n<th class=\"column-4\">2027</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody class=\"row-striping row-hover\">\r\n<tr class=\"row-2\">\r\n<td class=\"column-1\">New IMP work permit holder admissions</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-2\">285,750</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-3\">128,700</td>\r\n<td class=\"column-4\">155,700</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Many of the TEER 2 and TEER 3 occupations that still provide eligibility for SOWPs align with occupations in the Federal Economic Priorities bucket for planned admissions of new permanent residents: healthcare and trades.</p>', 'uploads/1737608898_Spousal Open Work Permits in Canada Navigating the New TEER Based Eligibility Requirements.webp', 'Spousal Open Work Permits in Canada', '2025-01-23', '2025-01-23 05:08:18', '2025-01-23 05:39:18'),
(123, 'Portugal Real Estate Market 2025 Why Its Europe Top Investment Destination', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\" The Portugal property scene remains in the spotlight as one of Europe\'s top spots for folks looking to grow their money. Whether the Portugal Golden Visa grabs you, the fancy homes going up, or just the sweet life in general, laying down cash for a Portugal spot in 2025 is a play that looks like it\'s gonna keep paying off. \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\" Portugal Real Estate Market 2025 Why Its Europe Top Investment Destination \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" The Portugal property scene remains in the spotlight as one of Europe\'s top spots for folks looking to grow their money. Whether the Portugal Golden Visa grabs you, the fancy homes going up, or just the sweet life in general, laying down cash for a Portugal spot in 2025 is a play that looks like it\'s gonna keep paying off. \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1737784049_Portugal%20Real%20Estate%20Market%202025%20Why%20Its%20Europe%20Top%20Investment%20Destination.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<h2 style=\"margin-bottom: 20px;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">&laquo; Portugal\'s Tough Real Estate Scene &raquo;</span></strong></h2>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Market Performance Against Other EU Nations</strong></h4>\r\n<p>When most European property areas, such as Germany and Finland, hit a slump or even fell in 2024, places like Portugal just kept climbing up. Numbers from Eurostat say house prices in Portugal got a 9.8% boost in just 2024\'s third chunk leaving other European places in the dust.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Things Making the Market Soar</strong></h4>\r\n<p>This upward move comes from a bunch of stuff: worldwide interest cool government perks including the Portugal Golden Visa, and solid money scenes. These bits have turned Portugal into this sweet spot for folks from abroad wanting to stack up their cash in a safe spot.</p>\r\n<h3 style=\"margin-bottom: 20px;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤ </span>Why Putting Your Money in Portugal Property Rocks</strong></h3>\r\n<h4><strong>▲&nbsp;It\'s Got Global Charm</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Portugal has turned into a hot spot for investors around the globe, thanks to its open-door policies stunning scenery, and top-notch living standards. With its gleaming beaches and deep-rooted cultural scene, this nation delivers a way of life that\'s got a global fan base.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Portugal Golden Visa Program</strong></h4>\r\n<p>A major draw is the <a href=\"../service/europe/portugal-golden-residence-visa-program/\">Portugal Golden Visa</a>. It hands out residency to non-EU folks if they make a big enough investment. This deal has caught the eyes of investors hailing from the US, UK, Pakistan, and more who want passage to Europe.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Tax Breaks for Overseas Investors</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Portugal offers sweet tax deals to folks from overseas through its Non-Habitual Residency program. It\'s a hit because it lets qualified people enjoy lower taxes, which is super tempting for buyers from around the globe.</p>\r\n<h3 style=\"margin-bottom: 20px;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤&nbsp;</span>Top Spots to Drop Cash on Property in Portugal</strong></h3>\r\n<h5><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b; font-size: 12pt;\">Lisbon - Where the Money\'s At</span></strong></h5>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ What\'s Up with Lisbon\'s Property Scene</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Lisbon\'s the place to be for chucking money into real estate if you\'re after the fancy stuff. Knight Frank tells us that Lisbon\'s on the list of Europe\'s top ten cities expecting a 4.5% jump in top-tier home prices by the time 2025 rolls around.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Building Lisbon\'s Future</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Lisbon&rsquo;s surrounding areas, like Set&uacute;bal, Amadora, and Montijo, are seeing big upgrades to their infrastructure. They\'re putting in better train connections growing the subway lines, and laying down fresh roadways. Folks are starting to want to buy up property around there because of this.</p>\r\n<h5><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b; font-size: 12pt;\">Porto - A Cool Mix of Old and New</span></strong></h5>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Porto&rsquo;s Popularity Is Soaring with International Buyers</strong></h4>\r\n<p>The city of Porto famous for its stunning UNESCO World Heritage spots, is turning into a hot pick for folks looking to invest. Come 2024 even investors from Saudi Arabia were showing they\'re into Porto signalling its rising star on the world map.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ What Makes Porto Real Estate Stand Out</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Porto blends old-timey charm with the latest comforts, which makes it just right for folks wanting the old and the new in their money-making ventures.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Algarve &ndash; The Sun-Soaked Haven</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Over in the Algarve, you\'ll find another prime spot for putting your cash into real estate. Its killer beaches top-notch golf spots, and always-nice weather are a dream for swanky homes and holiday stays.</p>\r\n<h3 style=\"margin-bottom: 20px;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤&nbsp;</span>Portugal\'s Golden Ticket to Living There and Other Perks</strong></h3>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Perks of Grabbing Portugal\'s Golden Visa</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Getting your hands on the Portugal Golden Visa comes with a bunch of pluses. You get to zip around the Schengen Zone without a visa, and you can snag permanent residency after hanging out for five years. It\'s a stepping stone to becoming a full-blown Portuguese citizen.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Who Can Go for It and How to Get Cracking</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Investors have a few choices to meet the qualifications, like putting money into property valued at a minimum of &euro;500,000 or chipping in a smaller sum of &euro;350,000 to help with city renewal efforts.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Portugal\'s Golden Visa Attracts Pakistani Nationals</strong></h4>\r\n<p>The Portugal Golden Visa has caught the attention of folks from Pakistan big time. It provides a no-fuss path to living in Europe, so it\'s no wonder it&rsquo;s pretty popular for those chasing after new chances.</p>\r\n<h3 style=\"margin-bottom: 20px;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤&nbsp;</span>Peeking Into 2024 and What 2025 Might Bring</strong></h3>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Highlights from the Eurostat Report</strong></h4>\r\n<p>The Eurostat report shines a light on how much Portugal\'s property prices keep climbing. They rose by 7% in early 2024, bumped up 7.8% in the following bit, and jumped a whole 9.8% by the third part of the year.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ What\'s Next for Portugal&rsquo;s Property Biz</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Brains in the biz are guessing Portugal\'s property scene will boost up by 5.8% in 2025. That\'s smokin&rsquo; compared to the rest of Europe\'s market, which might dip by about 2.5%.</p>\r\n<h3 style=\"margin-bottom: 20px;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤&nbsp;</span>Why Portugal\'s a Hot Ticket for Outsiders with Cash</strong></h3>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Staying Safe Soaking Up Sun, and Living It Up</strong></h4>\r\n<p>Portugal sits at number seven on the list of the world\'s safest countries providing a combo of security, sunshine, and high living standards. This combo turns Portugal into a top pick for both investors and expatriates.</p>\r\n<h4><strong>▲ Luxury Property Market on the Rise</strong></h4>\r\n<p>With a rep that keeps going up as a hotspot for fancy property, Portugal draws rich folks from places like the US, the UK, and Asia. They\'re all after homes that spell out comfort and are all about being exclusive.</p>\r\n<h4><strong><em>&bull; Wrapping It Up &bull;</em></strong></h4>\r\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portugal\">Portugal</a> property scene remains in the spotlight as one of Europe\'s top spots for folks looking to grow their money. Whether the Portugal Golden Visa grabs you, the fancy homes going up, or just the sweet life in general, laying down cash for a Portugal spot in 2025 is a play that looks like it\'s gonna keep paying off.</p>', 'uploads/1737784049_Portugal Real Estate Market 2025 Why Its Europe Top Investment Destination.webp', 'Portugal Real Estate', '2025-01-25', '2025-01-25 05:47:29', '2025-01-25 05:54:25');
INSERT INTO `news` (`id`, `title`, `metadata`, `news_detail`, `news_image`, `image_alt`, `news_date`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(124, 'Exploring Canada Open Work Permit OWP Extension for PNP Applicants', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\" The Canadian government\'s decision to give unrestricted work licenses to PNP candidates is a good one. Applicants may look for better career prospects while they wait for permanent residency. This new regulation makes it easier to obtain a Canadian immigration visa for anyone who wants to relocate to Canada through the PNP, benefiting everyone. \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\" Exploring Canada Open Work Permit OWP Extension for PNP Applicants \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" The Canadian government\'s decision to give unrestricted work licenses to PNP candidates is a good one. Applicants may look for better career prospects while they wait for permanent residency. This new regulation makes it easier to obtain a Canadian immigration visa for anyone who wants to relocate to Canada through the PNP, benefiting everyone. \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1738401682_Exploring%20Canada%20Open%20Work%20Permit%20OWP%20Extension%20for%20PNP%20Applicants.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Immigrants have&ensp;always been drawn to Canada, and the country is doing its utmost to bring in the right people and grow with them. <span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; color: #000000;\">New Policy for Open Work Permits to PNP Candidates Recently, the Canadian government has expanded one&ensp;of its initiatives to PNP candidates and their family members. The change aims to provide more work flexibility for those applying via the PNP while they wait&ensp;for their permanent residence</span><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-kerning: 0pt; mso-ligatures: none; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;\">.</span> </span>&nbsp;But how will this change benefit PNP candidates, and what will it mean for those wanting to&ensp;move to Canada? Let&rsquo;s take a closer look.</span></p>\r\n<h2><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">What is an Open Work Permit (OWP)?</span></strong></h2>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Before going into the particulars of the new policy,&ensp;it&rsquo;</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">s best to first understand</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> what an open work permit (OWP) is. An</span> <span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Open Work Permit (OWP) is a </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">type of</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> work permit that allows foreigners to work for&ensp;any employer in Canada. While employer-specific work&ensp;permits (closed work permits) tie workers to a specific job or employer, OWPs provide greater flexibility. Such flexibility is </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">especially important</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&ensp;for PNP candidates </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">as they move</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> towards permanent residency.</span></p>\r\n<h2><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">What is the Provincial Nominee Program (PNP)?</span></strong></h2>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">A Canadian immigration route known as the </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Provincial Nominee Program (PNP) allows provinces and territories to</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> designate individuals for permanent residency </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">on the basis of</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> their qualifications, work history, and capacity to support the local economy. It </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">has a close connection</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> to the <a href=\"../service/canadian-immigration-services/pnp-express-entry/\">Canada&nbsp;Express Entry</a> system, which oversees that group of economic immigration applicants. </span></p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤ </strong></span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">PNP Express Entry: A Pathway to Permanent Residency</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">The PNP, which underpins the Express Entry system, </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">is a critical component of the Canadian immigration system.</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> Express Entry is primarily used to handle </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">applications for the Federal Skilled Worker Program, Federal Skilled Trades Program, and</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> the Canadian Experience Class. Individuals nominated by a province can improve </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">their prospects of receiving an Invitation to Apply (ITA) for permanent residency</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> by earning points through the Comprehensive Ranking System (CRS) through Provincial Nominee Programs (PNP). </span></p>\r\n<h2><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Canadian New Policy on Work Permits for PNP Candidates</span></strong></h2>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Specifically, the new Canadian immigration policy seeks to make it easier for those applying through the PNP to find employment in Canada by issuing open work permits. These permits allow candidates to work with any employer&ensp;they want in Canada&nbsp;</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">whilst they wait</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> for their PR applications to be processed. The </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">change to&ensp;policy</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> is the latest effort to smooth the transition for PNP candidates from temporary to permanent status.</span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤</span> </strong><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Why is This Policy Important for PNP Candidates?</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">The main benefit of this new policy is the ability for PNP candidates to work freely across Canada. Previously, many PNP applicants were restricted to working for a specific employer </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">in a specific</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> job. With open work permits, they can take advantage of more job opportunities, thus improving their chances </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">of finding employment that suits their skills and interests.</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> This flexibility is not only beneficial for individuals but also for employers who may find it easier to hire foreign talent.</span></p>\r\n<h2><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">How Does the Policy Work?</span></strong></h2>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Let&rsquo;s explain how the open work permit process works for PNP applicants under the new policy.</span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Step 1:</span> Understand the Eligibility Requirements</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">To apply for an open work permit under the new policy, you </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">need to</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> be a nominee under the Provincial Nominee Program. You must also be in a position </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">where you are</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> waiting for your permanent residency application to be processed.</span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Step 2:</span> Prepare Your Application</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Once you&rsquo;ve verified that you&rsquo;re eligible, you will have to fill out an application for an&ensp;open work permit. The application is multi-staged: You </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">would need to</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> collect&ensp;certain documents like proof of your provincial nomination and information regarding your work experience.</span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Step 3:</span> Pay the Fees</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Just like most immigration applications, there is a&ensp;fee to </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">submit an application for an</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> open work permit. These are the work permit fee, open work permit holder fee, and, if needed, restoration of&ensp;status fee.</span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Step 4:</span> Submit Your Application Online</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">To apply, you have to re</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">gister with the IRCC Secure Account. This account&ensp;</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">enables you to</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> apply online, pay your fees, and track your application status.</span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Step 5:</span> Wait for Processing</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\"><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\">When you apply, however, you will await&ensp;processing</span><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\">.</span></span>&nbsp;</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Processing times can vary, so </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">it&rsquo;s </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">important</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> to check</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> your IRCC&ensp;Secure Account for updates.</span></p>\r\n<h2><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Benefits of Open Work Permits for PNP Candidates</span></strong></h2>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">The open work permit is </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">a great</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> benefit for PNP applicants. Some of the most notable of those were:</span></p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤ </strong></span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Flexibility in Employment</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">As discussed above, open work permits allow you to go to work for any employer in Canada.&nbsp;</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">This</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> is a </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">major</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> advantage over closed work permits, which only allow one to work for a specific&ensp;employer.</span></p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤ </strong></span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Opportunities to Gain Canadian Work Experience</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">More than work experience in Canada is&nbsp;</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">important</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> for the immigration process for PNP candidates. An open work permit allows you to do any job that matches your skills and qualifications, </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">and this will increase</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> your chances&ensp;of getting a permanent residence status.</span></p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤ </strong></span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Increased Earning Potential</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">On top of it all, being able to work&ensp;for whichever employer you want means the chance to negotiate better jobs that pay more. </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">This</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> can help </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">a lot</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> with your finances until you get your permanent residency.</span></p>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤ </strong></span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Access to Social Benefits</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Working in Canada under an open work permit means you will likely be eligible for Canadian social benefits such as healthcare and employment insurance, </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">which will provide peace of mind as you wait</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> for your permanent residency.</span></p>\r\n<h2><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">How to Apply for an Open Work Permit (OWP) as a PNP Candidate</span></strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤ </strong></span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Step-by-Step Application Process</span></strong></h3>\r\n<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&bull; <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Sign Up for an IRCC Secure Account:</span><br></span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Make sure</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> you\'ve uploaded all the necessary files by regularly reviewing the document checklist.</span></p>\r\n<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&bull; <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Pay the Necessary Fees:</span><br></span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Make sure</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> you\'ve uploaded all the </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">necessary files</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> by </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">regularly</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> reviewing the document checklist.</span></p>\r\n<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&bull; <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Complete the Application Form:</span><br></span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">You must complete the application, make sure all the fields are accurate, and upload the required files.</span></p>\r\n<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&bull; <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Submit Your Application:</span><br></span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">You must complete the application, make sure all the fields are accurate, and upload the </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">required</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> files.</span></p>\r\n<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&bull; <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Receive Your Work Permit:</span><br></span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif; color: #000000;\">You must complete the application, make sure all the fields are accurate, and upload the required files.</span></p>\r\n<h2><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">What Documents Are Needed for the Application?</span></strong></h2>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">When applying for an open work permit through the PNP, you </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">will need to</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> upload certain documents. These may include:</span></p>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">▲</span> A valid passport<br></span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">▲</span> A Family Information Form (IMM 5707)<br></span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">▲</span> A digital photo<br></span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">▲</span> A support letter from the province or territory<br></span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">▲</span> A copy of your most recent work permit (if applicable)</span></p>\r\n<h2><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Common Mistakes to Avoid</span></strong></h2>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Applying for an open work permit under the PNP program can be a complex process, and there are a few common mistakes that applicants should avoid:</span></p>\r\n<p><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Incomplete Application Forms:</span></span></strong> <span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Make sure the form is </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">completely</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> filled out, as some information must&ensp;be present for the</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> process, oth</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">erwise it will be delayed.<br></span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Failure to Pay Fees:</span></span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> Ensure that you have received a receipt of payment, as your application cannot be processed&ensp;unless the payment is complete</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">.<br></span><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Missing Documents:</span></span></strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> You </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">have to</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> fill out the application, upload the necessary files, and confirm that all the fields are correct.</span></p>\r\n<h4><em><strong><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">Conclusion: A Step Forward for PNP Candidates</span></strong></em></h4>\r\n<p><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">The Canadian government\'s decision to give unrestricted work licenses to PNP candidates is</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> a </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">good </span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">one</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">.</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\"> Applicants may look for better career prospects while they wait for permanent residency</span><span data-preserver-spaces=\"true\">. This new regulation makes it easier to obtain a <a href=\"../service/canadian-immigration-services/\">Canadian immigration</a> visa for anyone who wants to relocate to Canada through the PNP, benefiting everyone.</span></p>', 'uploads/1738401682_Exploring Canada Open Work Permit OWP Extension for PNP Applicants.webp', 'Canada Open Work Permit OWP', '2025-02-01', '2025-02-01 09:21:22', '2025-02-01 09:24:23'),
(125, 'Celebrating 10 Years of Express Entry A Decade of Immigration Innovation in Canada', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\" Since its inception in 2015, Express Entry has undergone substantial change. The system\'s focus on efficiency, flexibility, and merit-based selection has helped Canada attract skilled workers from around the world to meet labor market demands. \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\" Celebrating 10 Years of Express Entry A Decade of Immigration Innovation in Canada \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" Since its inception in 2015, Express Entry has undergone substantial change. The system\'s focus on efficiency, flexibility, and merit-based selection has helped Canada attract skilled workers from around the world to meet labor market demands. \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1738994875_Celebrating%2010%20Years%20of%20Express%20Entry%20A%20Decade%20of%20Immigration%20Innovation%20in%20Canada.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<h2 class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 18pt; color: #c1915b;\"><strong><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\">Canada\'s Express Entry System: Celebrating <span style=\"color: #000000;\">10</span> <span style=\"color: #000000;\">Years</span> of Immigration Innovation</span></strong></span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">January 31, 2025, marks the tenth anniversary of Canada\'s groundbreaking Express Entry system, which has transformed the country\'s immigration landscape since its launch in 2015. Under this innovative, pool-based system, Immigration, Refugees, and Citizenship Canada (IRCC) have issued more than 800,000 Invitations to Apply (ITAs) for Permanent Residency (PR) to foreign nationals over the past decade.<br><br>Express Entry has fundamentally altered Canada\'s immigration application process, making it more responsive to labor market demands and commercial interests. Because it has made the path to permanent residence faster, more accessible, and more effective, professionals from all over the world can now contribute to Canada\'s economy. This article examines the evolution of Express Entry, its key characteristics, and its continued impact on immigration policy in Canada.</span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤</span> </strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\">Why Was Express Entry Created?</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Before Express Entry, Canada used a first-come, first-served system for skilled worker applications. In the old system, eligible foreign people could apply for permanent residence (PR) and would be considered permanent residents after their petitions were processed. However, this strategy led to lengthy processing times and massive backlogs. In the past, it may take up to seven years to process a PR application. Applicants frequently found that they were waiting so long that they were no longer qualified for the employment they first qualified for due to changes in their personal or professional circumstances. <br><br>To address these challenges, the Canadian government launched the Express Entry program in January 2015. Express Entry sought to reform Canada\'s immigration system by using a more straightforward, merit-based selection procedure. This made it possible for the Canadian government to manage the backlog, adapt to shifting labor market demands, and ensure that applications are processed promptly. </span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤ </span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\">How Express Entry Changed Canada\'s Immigration System</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Express Entry substantially cut processing times and raised the system\'s efficiency by introducing a pool-based approach for handling applications for Permanent Residency (PR) from trained personnel. Those hoping to get PR first build an Expression of Interest (EOI) profile within the Express Entry pool. The Comprehensive Ranking System (CRS) gives points based on elements, including their profiles\' ranking. </span></p>\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Age<br></span></strong><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Education<br></span></strong><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Language proficiency<br></span></strong><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Work experience</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">The highest CRS candidates are asked to apply for PR via IRCC\'s regular drawings. This approach helps to guarantee short processing times and prioritizes the most qualified candidates. Actually, successful applicants under Express Entry should normally expect their applications to be handled in six months, which is a notable change from the previous method.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">This system\'s primary benefit is that it lets provinces and companies choose individuals from the Express Entry pool who would be most fit to cover labor market shortages. Applications for four primary economic immigration programs are handled by the initiative: </span></p>\r\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Federal Skilled Worker Program (FSWP)<br></span></strong><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Federal Skilled Trades Program (FSTP)<br></span></strong><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Canadian Experience Class (CEC)<br></span></strong><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Provincial Nominee Program (PNP)</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">By use of these initiatives, qualified professionals from all around the world can apply for PR, their eligibility decided by objective criteria including work experience and education. </span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤&nbsp;</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\">Key Changes in Express Entry Over the Last 10 Years</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Express Entry has changed significantly since its launch in 2015 in response to changes in Canada\'s immigration policies, labor market, and economic demands. These changes have increased the system\'s flexibility and inclusiveness. Some of the most important modifications are below: </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">ⅰ. <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Job Offers and CRS Points</span></span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Early on in <a href=\"../service/canadian-immigration-services/pnp-express-entry/\">Express Entry</a>, candidates with genuine employment offers in Canada received 600 extra CRS points, which frequently helped to produce high CRS cut-off values in the early drawings. But in 2016, the government instituted \"target\" improvements \"to the\" system that cut the points given for employment offers.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Under the changed method, candidates with job offers in some National Occupational Classification (NOC) categories gained 50 or 200 extra points based on the NOC code of the position. This modification sought to balance and fairly operate the system. The Canadian government declared that all job offer points would be removed from the CRS by December 2024; the expected effect would be seen in the Spring of 2025. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">ⅱ. <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Educational Credentials</span></span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">The CRS also began awarding points based on a candidate&rsquo;s education. Starting in 2016, candidates were awarded additional CRS points for holding diplomas, degrees, or certificates from recognized institutions.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Candidates could earn:</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; 15 points for a one- to two-year diploma or certificate.<br></span><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; 30 points for a degree, diploma, or certificate of three years or longer.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">This change reflected Canada&rsquo;s increasing focus on attracting highly educated immigrants to meet the country&rsquo;s growing skilled labor.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">ⅲ. <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Tie-breaking Rule</span></span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">In 2017, IRCC implemented a tie-breaking rule to address scenarios where more candidates met the CRS cut-off score than there were invitations available. The rule used the submission date and time of candidate profiles to determine which applicants would be invited to apply. Candidates who submitted their profiles earlier would be given priority in the case of a tie, ensuring fairness in the selection process.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">ⅳ. <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">French Language Proficiency</span></span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">The addition of extra points for applicants who showed fluency in French was another noteworthy modification in 2017. If a French speaker performs well on all four French language skills&mdash;speaking, listening, reading, and writing - they receive extra CRS points. Candidates can earn up to 30 extra CRS points if they score 7 or higher on these skills and have a strong grasp of English (CLB 5 or higher). <br><br>The purpose of this reform was to help recruit French-speaking immigrants to fill Canada\'s labor shortage, especially in non-Quebec provinces where there is a considerable demand for French speakers.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">ⅴ. <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Siblings in Canada</span></span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Additional CRS points were added by the IRCC in 2017 for applicants who, or their accompanying spouse, had a sibling who was a Canadian citizen or permanent resident. The goal of this action was to improve family ties and facilitate immigrants\' easier assimilation into Canadian society.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">ⅵ. <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">Category-based Selection</span></span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">The IRCC implemented category-based selection in 2023, which enables draws to concentrate on particular economic sectors like commerce, transportation, healthcare, STEM (science, technology, engineering, and math) vocations, and agriculture. The purpose of this modification was to draw applicants with experience in in-demand disciplines and to address labor shortages in particular industries. Because the CRS cut-off scores for these focused draws were lower than those for general draws, it was simpler for people with specialized abilities to be eligible for PR.</span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤&nbsp;</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\">Impact of the COVID-19 Pandemic on Express Entry</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Express Entry and other forms of immigration to Canada were significantly impacted by the COVID-19 outbreak. While draws for candidates in the Canadian Experience Class and Provincial Nominee Program continued, the IRCC halted general draws for approximately 18 months during the early phases of the epidemic. CRS scores varied as a result of this suspension; some drawings, like the February 2021 CEC draw, which invited 27,332 candidates with a cut-off CRS score of only 75, had exceptionally low cut-off scores. <br><br>In July 2022, IRCC restarted general drawings and made adjustments to meet the growing demand for skilled workers as the pandemic subsided and Canada adapted to new travel restrictions.</span></p>\r\n<h3><strong><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">➤&nbsp;</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><strong><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\">Recent Developments and Future Outlook</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">In May 2024, the IRCC began holding more targeted draws for certain areas, like healthcare and French-language proficiency, with an emphasis on in-Canada candidates. This shift is anticipated to continue as the Canadian government seeks to reduce the number of non-permanent residents in the nation. <br><br>The Immigration Levels Plan 2025-2027 pledged to place greater emphasis on in-Canada applications with the goal of giving precedence to those who are already residing in Canada. This action aligns with the administration\'s goal of converting temporary residents into permanent residents. <br><br>Additionally, the federal government is increasing the amount of Express Entry allotments, as evidenced by the 2025&ndash;2027 levels plan. The continued importance of Express Entry in Canada\'s immigration policy is highlighted by the fact that it accounts for a greater portion of the overall economic immigration budget. </span></p>\r\n<h4 class=\"MsoNormal\"><em><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%;\">Conclusion</span></strong></em></h4>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 107%; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\">Since its inception in 2015, Express Entry has undergone substantial change. The system\'s focus on efficiency, flexibility, and merit-based selection has helped Canada attract <a href=\"../skilled-semi-skilled/\">skilled workers</a> from around the world to meet labor market demands. As the immigration landscape evolves, Express Entry will continue to be a key tool in ensuring that Canada can sustain a high level of economic growth and prosperity. Because of ongoing enhancements and a focus on specific industries and applications, Express Entry is well-positioned to play a significant role in deciding Canada\'s immigration future for years to come.</span></p>', 'uploads/1738994875_Celebrating 10 Years of Express Entry A Decade of Immigration Innovation in Canada.webp', 'Express Entry', '2025-02-08', '2025-02-08 06:07:55', '2025-02-08 06:09:04'),
(126, 'Australia Subclass 491 Visa Updates 2024 and 25 Everything You Need to Know', '<meta name=\"description\" content=\" The Subclass 491 Visa remains a popular pathway for skilled workers to settle in regional Australia. However, backlogs and processing delays continue to challenge applicants. \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\" Australia Subclass 491 Visa Updates 2024 - 25 Everything You Need to Know \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:description\" The Subclass 491 Visa remains a popular pathway for skilled workers to settle in regional Australia. However, backlogs and processing delays continue to challenge applicants. \" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"Lalani Associates\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:publisher\" content=\"https://www.facebook.com/LalaniAssociates/\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2024-08-03T02:30:00+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2024-07-30T06:58:49+00:00\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://lalaniassociates.com/Admin/uploads/1739178319_Australia%20Subclass%20491%20Visa%20Updates%202024%20to%2025%20Everything%20You%20Need%20to%20Know.webp\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1250\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"754\" />\r\n<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/webp\" />\r\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@lalaniassoc\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"admin\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" />\r\n<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"2 minutes\" />', '<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">Australia&rsquo;s immigration landscape is witnessing crucial changes, especially concerning the <strong>Subclass 491 Skilled Work Regional (Provisional) Visa</strong>. For the <strong>2024-25 fiscal year</strong>, the Australian government has allocated <strong>33,000 regional visas</strong>, with <strong>28,500 visas</strong> specifically dedicated to the <a href=\"../service/australian-immigration-services/australian-skilled-worker/\">subclass 491 visa</a>. However, a significant backlog and shifting processing priorities have created uncertainty for many applicants.</p>\r\n<p>If you are planning to apply for the <strong>Subclass 491 Visa</strong>, staying informed about the latest updates is crucial. In this article, we will break down recent trends, pending applications, processing times, and what applicants should expect in the coming months.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Subclass 491 Visa Updates for <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\">2024-25</span></strong></h2>\r\n<p>The Australian government has implemented significant changes to streamline the visa allocation process:</p>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Total regional visas available</strong>: <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>33,000</strong></span></p>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Subclass 491 Visa allocation</strong>: <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>28,500</strong></span></p>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Applications approved so far</strong>: <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>15,652</strong></span></p>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&bull; Remaining available visas</strong>: <span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>12,398</strong></span></p>\r\n<p>Additionally, the government plans to prioritize <strong>10% of visas</strong> for <strong>high-demand occupations</strong> and another <strong>10% for complex cases</strong>, leaving <strong>11,158 visas</strong> for standard processing.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Recent Trends in Subclass 491 Visa Grants</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤ </strong></span><strong>Monthly Subclass 491 Visa Grant Trends</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Recent data indicates a fluctuating trend in visa grants:</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Month</th>\r\n<th>Subclass 491 Visa Grants Issued</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>July 2024</td>\r\n<td>4,179</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>August 2024</td>\r\n<td>3,237</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>September 2024</td>\r\n<td>3,375</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>October 2024</td>\r\n<td>1,609</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>November 2024</td>\r\n<td>2,078</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>December 2024</td>\r\n<td>1,174</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The decline in visa grants has significantly affected <strong>offshore applicants</strong>, leading to prolonged processing times.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Backlogs and Pending Applications by Year</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤&nbsp;</strong></span><strong>Applications Pending from Previous Years</strong></h3>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>2022 Pending Applications</strong></span></h4>\r\n<p>Although the majority of <strong>2022 applications</strong> have been processed, <strong>some remain unprocessed</strong>:</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Lodgment Month</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Pending Applications</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>January 2022</td>\r\n<td>5</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>December 2022</td>\r\n<td>124</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>2023 Pending Applications</strong></span></h4>\r\n<p>The largest backlog stems from <strong>2023 applications</strong>, with <strong>13,694 still pending</strong>.</p>\r\n<h4><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>2024 Pending Applications</strong></span></h4>\r\n<p>There are <strong>10,727 applications</strong> still under processing from <strong>2024</strong>, with <strong>December 2024</strong> having the highest backlog.</p>\r\n<h2><strong>Processing Updates and Trends</strong></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤&nbsp;</strong></span><strong>Subclass 491 Visa Processing for 2023</strong></h3>\r\n<p>The number of processed applications in <strong>2023</strong> saw a <strong>sharp increase between May and June</strong>:</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Month</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Applications Processed</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>May 2023</td>\r\n<td>215</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>June 2023</td>\r\n<td>481</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h3><span style=\"color: #c1915b;\"><strong>➤&nbsp;</strong></span><strong>Subclass 491 Visa Processing for 2024</strong></h3>\r\n<p>Processing in <strong>2024</strong> has slowed, likely due to shifting priorities:</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Month</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Applications Processed</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>October 2024</td>\r\n<td>71</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>November 2024</td>\r\n<td>60</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>December 2024</td>\r\n<td>10</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<h2><strong>Future Outlook for Subclass 491 Visa Applicants</strong></h2>\r\n<p>With <strong>only 12,398 visas remaining</strong>, applicants must ensure their applications are complete, error-free, and meet priority occupation criteria. Seeking <strong>professional assistance</strong> can increase the chances of approval.</p>\r\n<h4><em><strong>Conclusion</strong></em></h4>\r\n<p>The <strong>Subclass 491 Visa</strong> remains a popular pathway for <a href=\"../news/Skilled-Work-Regional-Visa-491-Everything-You-Need-to-Know\">skilled workers</a> to settle in regional <a href=\"https://www.homeaffairs.gov.au/\">Australia</a>. However, backlogs and processing delays continue to challenge applicants. Understanding the latest trends, prioritizing high-demand occupations, and ensuring a <strong>strong application</strong> will be essential for success in <strong>2024-25</strong>.</p>', 'uploads/1739178319_Australia Subclass 491 Visa Updates 2024 to 25 Everything You Need to Know.webp', 'Australia Subclass 491 Visa', '2025-02-10', '2025-02-10 09:05:19', '2025-02-10 09:07:18');
